<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     ASYMPTOTIC STAT MACROS — replaces fixed ± deltas with proportional
     changes so low stats can recover meaningfully and high stats fall
     hard. Gains scale with HEADROOM (100 - current); losses scale with
     CURRENT. N is the old fixed-delta value, now read as a "percent
     intensity" (so the old "+ 10" becomes "($statGain: $stat, 10)" —
     a 10% headroom gain). Results are clamped to 0..100 and rounded
     so the stat bar shows clean integers.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
(set: $statGain to (macro: num-type _v, num-type _n, [(output-data: (round: (min: 100, _v + (100 - _v) * (_n / 50))))]))
<!-- 2026-10-29 (Sam, playtest notes 3 and 4: the bars "get very low very fast. I think they should be gated above the point where they have any effect on options until you complete the errand and give Inis page 93"): until $returnedPage, a loss stops at 40, above every flagging slip (under 40) and every option gate (under 30); a stat already under 40 is not lifted -->(set: $statLoss to (macro: num-type _v, num-type _n, [(output-data: (max: (cond: $returnedPage is true, 0, (min: _v, 40)), (round: (max: 0, _v - _v * (_n / 50)))))]))\
<!-- Flat costs for the acts that must bite whoever you are (2026-09-28, Sam: "Do that"): a fixed number of points, clamped to 0..100. Ordinary beats keep the proportional helpers above. -->
(set: $statCut to (macro: num-type _v, num-type _n, [(output-data: (round: (max: 0, _v - _n)))]))\
(set: $statLift to (macro: num-type _v, num-type _n, [(output-data: (round: (min: 100, _v + _n)))]))
<!-- ─── v2 EXPANSION: dream-worlds via Three Pillars ────────────────────
