(go-to: "Dean Street")

:: The Phone Box [outdoor street-night] {"position":"1400,300","size":"100,100"}
<!-- THE PHONE BOX (2026-09-13). Sam's idea: every phone in this game rings AT
     you and you either take it or say you are not here. You can never ring out.
     This is the one place you can, and the only person you would ring is Aoife.
     It takes the Donkey coin, which until now had exactly one use (the flip at
     the Colony Room Door) and a pickup line promising "You'll want it later"
     that nothing ever paid off. Spending it here buys back ONE refused call:
     $refusedCalls comes down by one, so the Fetch omen at two refusals recedes.
     Spending it here also means you will not have it to flip at the Colony
     doors. That is the trade and it is meant to be felt.
     The dual ring is NOT recoverable: once $refusedDualRing is set LILY does not
     ring again that night and the box cannot buy that call back; it says so.
     Since 2026-10-11 (Sam) turning her away is a glimpse of the Fetch, not a meeting. -->
(set: $alleyReturn to true)\
(display: "Key Guards")\
<!-- 2026-10-11 structure pass 3: the small lift comes on the first visit only; stepping in and out of the box paid it every time. -->(unless: (history:) contains "The Phone Box")[(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 2))]\

(if: $hasCoin is false)[<div>You have no coin.</div>
]\
<!-- 2026-10-11 (Sam, "Restore it"): his line for the refused dual ring, cut on 10 October while that refusal ended the night; reachable again now it is a glimpse. -->(else-if: $refusedDualRing is true)[<div>Too late to ring her now.</div>
]\
(else-if: $refusedCalls > 0)[<div>You have one coin, the Donkey you found earlier. You could call AOIFE.</div>

(link: "Put the coin in and dial")[(set: $hasCoin to false)(set: $refusedCalls to $refusedCalls - 1)\
<div>It rings twice. AOIFE answers.</div>
<div class="inventory-note">THE DONKEY SPENT &#183; ONE CALL TAKEN BACK</div>
]]\

[[Back to Dean Street|Dean Street]]

:: Approach Shana [venue-trishas] {"position":"700,1700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="trishas-frame">
<span class="trishas-strip">(display: "Trisha Strip SVG")</span>
<!-- $metShana now set in "Shana Reads" — setting it on render here meant a
     declined reading still closed Trisha's on the hub -->
Her lovers are always speechless, beautiful women; her male companions keep a tonsured silence.

She doesn’t look up but knows you’re there because she has read the Angelic Keys of Edward Kelly, and has such a talent for practical magick. Drinks land on the table, all whiskies, one for each of her five companions and somehow one more for you. She is yet to look up.

‘Give it here,’ she says.

<span class="guided-link">[[Hand over the manuscript|Shana Reads]]</span>
[[Not yet.|Trisha's]]

:: Approach the novelist [venue-french char-novelist] {"position":"500,550","size":"100,100"}
(display: "French Rule SVG h60")
(display: "French Reentry")

Between the ground you’ve taken and his position falls an amber monolith, through the window onto Dean Street; a thick and molten bar on the gnarly floor, light and apart. If you lingered in it you’d become a fossil, like the filoplume of a silent dinosaur.

You once told him that he should stick to poems.

What have you got to lose?

<div class="french-lose-choices">
[[Nothing|The novelist]]
<!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam, A): "Everything" also leads into his reading and THE REFUSAL, at a higher price than "Nothing" (6 more morale; the reading takes its own 9) -->(link: "Everything")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 6))(go-to: "The novelist")]
</div>

(display: "French Rule SVG h24")</svg>

:: Approach The French [outdoor] {"position":"1100,300","size":"100,100"}
(set: $frenchApproached to true)\
<div class="approach-back">[[← Back to Dean Street|Dean Street]]</div>
<div id="fh-container"></div>[[·|The French]]
(display: "Stash Point")

:: Approach The Coach [outdoor] {"position":"1100,1400","size":"100,100"}
<div class="approach-back">[[← Back to Dean Street|Dean Street]]</div>
<div id="ch-container"></div><!-- Sam 2026-10-07: walking in by the front door takes you to the bar; only a blackout lands you in the gents. 2026-10-08: on the locked path (hut burnt) the door does not open; the pub is only there to burn. -->(if: $hutBurnt is true)[<span data-coach-locked></span>(if: $coachBurnt is false and $brokenWindows's length < 3)[<div data-coach-wait>There is the Coach and Horses. It looks, in this thin-blooded light, like so much ready kindling.

Mr. Vladimir spoke truly, in an ideal world you’d toss a bomb into the heart of pure mathematics. Yes, Mr. Konrad, THAT is impossible! So why not kill a pub instead?

Kill its sordid history and your own past involving it; they clag like pavement gum on your Cuban heels. That, at least, would end the whole show cleanly. Smash some windows now and clamber in.</div>]](else-if: $coachUrgent is true)[[[·|Coach and Horses lock]]](else:)[(link: "·")[(set: $coachViaGents to false)<!-- 2026-10-22 (ordering audit, pass 3): midnight is parked (StoryInit, 2026-10-09: while $midnightEnabled is false midnight never falls, the date strap stays 23.11.73 and the Ham's rumour is never cut off). This front-door set was unguarded, so every cow or key visit flipped the date, fired the midnight caption and silenced the rumour; the gents' own set has carried this guard since the parking. -->(if: $midnightEnabled is true)[(set: $afterMidnight to true)](go-to: "Coach and Horses bar")]]
(if: $hutBurnt is true and $coachBurnt is false and $brokenWindows's length >= 3 and $visitedCentrePoint is false)[<div><span data-coach-fire-start>[[Burn it|The Coach Burns]]</span></div>]
(display: "Stash Point")

