:: At the Corner of Dean Street and Greek Street [outdoor char-red] {"position":"1200,400","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Ginger light -->
<div class="ginger-lamp-wrap">
<svg width="96" height="168" viewBox="0 0 96 168"><defs><radialGradient id="glGlow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#ffb43c" stop-opacity="0.55"/><stop offset="0.35" stop-color="#ff9a1e" stop-opacity="0.22"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#ff8c14" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient><radialGradient id="glPane" cx="50%" cy="45%" r="55%"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#fff0b8"/><stop offset="0.3" stop-color="#ffc24a"/><stop offset="0.75" stop-color="#e07a10" stop-opacity="0.85"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#8a3c04" stop-opacity="0.6"/></radialGradient><linearGradient id="glIron" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#3a2810"/><stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#6a4a1c"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#2a1a06"/></linearGradient></defs><ellipse cx="48" cy="46" rx="48" ry="40" fill="url(#glGlow)"/><path d="M48,2 L51,7 L48,12 L45,7 Z" fill="#5a3a10"/><rect x="46.5" y="11" width="3" height="4" fill="#2a1a06"/><path d="M28,20 Q48,12 68,20 L64,26 L32,26 Z" fill="#2a1a06"/><path d="M30,20 Q48,14 66,20" fill="none" stroke="#c8a86a" stroke-width="0.6" opacity="0.7"/><path d="M32,26 L64,26 L60,66 L36,66 Z" fill="url(#glPane)"/><path d="M32,26 L64,26 L60,66 L36,66 Z" fill="none" stroke="#2a1a06" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M48,26 L48,66 M33.2,38 L62.8,38 M34.4,52 L61.6,52" stroke="#2a1a06" stroke-width="1.1"/><path d="M40,29 L38.8,40 M41,56 L40.4,63" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.35)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-linecap="round"/><ellipse cx="48" cy="46" rx="6" ry="9" fill="#fff4c8" opacity="0.75"/><ellipse cx="48" cy="45" rx="2.6" ry="4.2" fill="#ffffff" opacity="0.9"/><rect x="34" y="66" width="28" height="5" rx="1.5" fill="#2a1a06"/><rect x="40" y="71" width="16" height="4" rx="1" fill="#5a3a10"/><path d="M30,80 L66,80" stroke="#5a3a10" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M30,80 q-4,-4 0,-8 M66,80 q4,-4 0,-8" fill="none" stroke="#5a3a10" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M44,75 L44,86 Q48,90 52,86 L52,75" fill="url(#glIron)" stroke="#2a1a06" stroke-width="0.6"/><rect x="44.5" y="88" width="7" height="60" rx="1.5" fill="url(#glIron)" stroke="#2a1a06" stroke-width="0.5"/><path d="M47,90 L47,146 M49.5,90 L49.5,146" stroke="rgba(255,220,160,0.14)" stroke-width="0.8"/><path d="M42,148 L54,148 L56,154 L40,154 Z" fill="#5a3a10"/><path d="M38,154 L58,154 L60,162 L36,162 Z" fill="#2a1a06"/><rect x="34" y="162" width="28" height="4" rx="1" fill="#2a1a06"/><path d="M45,88 L45,146" stroke="rgba(255,180,80,0.35)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round"/><ellipse cx="48" cy="166" rx="30" ry="2.4" fill="rgba(255,160,60,0.12)"/></svg>
</div>
<div class="ginger-scene">
<div class="ginger-light"></div>
A man, not much past twenty, stands under a ginger light. At first you think he must be a dilly boy. He wears a beret and paints his nails; he is epicene and crinoline, as if he might snap at any moment.

Then you clock him for a poet that you know. A poet called RED.

Like a tiger that moves in the Taiga, whose footprints fill as soon as they are made, what RED leaves of himself on the street is trackless at your shutter-speed; in proximity he gives an impression of the weightless bergs of ash he calves into the puddle at his feet, which, even as they should extinguish are, by some feeling wind, awakened to a transitory brightness.

You stand nearby for a while; he is somewhere elsewhere, vast.

[[Speak to him|You speak to the poet]]
</div>

:: Beaten [venue-cellar char-john char-salvu] {"position":"2200,1250","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Swinging bulb -->
<div class="cellar-bulb-wrap">
<svg width="48" height="90" viewBox="0 0 48 90"><!-- Wire from ceiling --><line x1="24" y1="0" x2="24" y2="30" stroke="#888878" stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.75"/><!-- Socket cap --><rect x="17" y="28" width="14" height="10" rx="2.5"fill="rgba(80,78,65,0.9)" stroke="rgba(160,155,120,0.7)" stroke-width="1"/><!-- Socket ring detail --><rect x="19" y="36" width="10" height="3" rx="1"fill="none" stroke="rgba(150,145,110,0.55)" stroke-width="0.8"/><!-- Outer glow halo --><ellipse cx="24" cy="60" rx="20" ry="22"fill="rgba(255,245,160,0.12)"/><!-- Bulb body — pear shape, bright and solid --><path d="M24,38 C16,38 10,45 10,55 C10,67 16,78 24,78 C32,78 38,67 38,55 C38,45 32,38 24,38 Z"fill="rgba(255,252,210,0.95)" stroke="rgba(220,210,160,0.6)" stroke-width="0.8"/><!-- Inner warm core --><ellipse cx="24" cy="57" rx="9" ry="11"fill="rgba(255,240,120,0.55)"/><!-- Filament — W-shape --><path d="M18,60 L20,53 L24,58 L28,53 L30,60"fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,200,40,0.95)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/><!-- Neck base ring --><rect x="20" y="75" width="8" height="3" rx="1"fill="rgba(200,195,155,0.65)" stroke="none"/></svg>
</div>
<div class="cellar-scene">
<div class="cellar-light"></div>
(set: $wasBeaten to true)
(if: $crossed is "john")[(set: $savedBy to "nobody")](else-if: $crossed is "ashton")[(set: $savedBy to "ashton")](else:)[(set: $savedBy to "john")]\
(if: $savedBy is "john")[
‘I don’t talk to liars,’ he roars, when a voice hollers from the staircase:

‘SALVU! Leave it! He’s alright.’ It’s JOHN ST. JOHN. ‘I know him. I don’t like the bloke but he’s sound.’

ST. JOHN’S face is legible only to you, who once knew him so well. He’s both amused at your straits and miffed that it falls upon him once again to rescue you.

(if: $metRed is true and $crossed is not "red")[He leans close as he pulls you to your feet: ‘RED told COPPER you had money.’ You’re lucky, you reflect, that COPPER could work out you don’t.]
(if: $crossed is "red")[He heard you rat on RED and it seems you impressed him.]

(if: $knowsCopperWord)[COPPER turns his back.

‘Well,’ says JOHN. ‘That went better than anyone expected.’

[[Back to Dean Street|The dark pass]]]
(else:)[[[He has something to tell you|St. John's Word]]]
](else-if: $savedBy is "ashton")[<span class="dss-no-john"></span>(set: $holdsAshtonName to true)
COPPER, fretful lion, shakes his jowls. ASHTON whispers something in his ear that seems to overfill him presto with a newly minted calm; such dreadful service must her lips have paid.

‘Maybe I rang customs,’ says ASHTON, the grinning tease. If she meant to confess then this is how she’d do it; but you can’t be sure what she means; you can’t even be sure that she knows what she means.

[[Up the stairs|The dark pass]]
](else:)[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 12))<span class="dss-no-john"></span>
COPPER roars in the stairwell and shakes his jowls. His strength is in the singularity of revealed violence. Like all Godfathers he can stand alone; the firm’s a means to hurry things along or shift the blame. Just as the debt stands, so, at length, do you.

[[Up the stairs|The dark pass]]
]
</div>

:: St. John's Word [venue-cellar char-john] {"position":"2200,1350","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Swinging bulb -->
<div class="cellar-bulb-wrap">
<svg width="48" height="90" viewBox="0 0 48 90"><!-- Wire from ceiling --><line x1="24" y1="0" x2="24" y2="30" stroke="#888878" stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.75"/><!-- Socket cap --><rect x="17" y="28" width="14" height="10" rx="2.5"fill="rgba(80,78,65,0.9)" stroke="rgba(160,155,120,0.7)" stroke-width="1"/><!-- Socket ring detail --><rect x="19" y="36" width="10" height="3" rx="1"fill="none" stroke="rgba(150,145,110,0.55)" stroke-width="0.8"/><!-- Outer glow halo --><ellipse cx="24" cy="60" rx="20" ry="22"fill="rgba(255,245,160,0.12)"/><!-- Bulb body — pear shape, bright and solid --><path d="M24,38 C16,38 10,45 10,55 C10,67 16,78 24,78 C32,78 38,67 38,55 C38,45 32,38 24,38 Z"fill="rgba(255,252,210,0.95)" stroke="rgba(220,210,160,0.6)" stroke-width="0.8"/><!-- Inner warm core --><ellipse cx="24" cy="57" rx="9" ry="11"fill="rgba(255,240,120,0.55)"/><!-- Filament — W-shape --><path d="M18,60 L20,53 L24,58 L28,53 L30,60"fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,200,40,0.95)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/><!-- Neck base ring --><rect x="20" y="75" width="8" height="3" rx="1"fill="rgba(200,195,155,0.65)" stroke="none"/></svg>
</div>
<div class="cellar-scene">
<div class="cellar-light"></div>
(if: $knowsCopperSecret is false)[‘LACKLAND’S got a hidden room. The word’s //Valletta//,’ says JOHN as he marshals you out.](else:)[‘LACKLAND’S got a hidden room. You know the word already,’ says JOHN as he marshals you out.]

‘Next time knock on the right door.’
(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 9))
(if: $knowsCopperSecret is false)[(set: $knowsCopperSecret to true)
(display: "Office Opens Line")
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">PASSWORD LEARNED</div>
<div class="item-name">“Valletta”</div>
<div class="item-note">It&#39;s saved in your notebook <span class="item-note-arrow">&#8593;</span></div>
</div>]

You surface to Dean Street.

[[Dean Street|The dark pass]]
</div>

