:: The Harp's Alley [outdoor] {"position":"300,1570","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-25 (Sam): the meeting in Brydges Place with the old friend from the Green Sea, an undercover man for the security services who is Heat and the Professor at once (Conrad, The Secret Agent). Three beats: he reads your night back (here), the two faces and the ask (Harp Alley Ask, Harp Alley Answer), the hand in his pocket (Harp Alley Standoff, Harp Alley End). Every pink line is a slot for Sam's own text, with a line from The Secret Agent under it to riff on (Project Gutenberg text, chapter given); the branching is built on the ship thread ($shipFate, $shipNews, $shipCall, $ashtonSold) and the cellar's $crossed. Once a game: $harpMet shuts the hub's Cecil Court door again. Stakes (stats, the Debt, a haunt) are not yet decided, so no beat moves a meter. -->
(set: $harpMet to true)\
<span class="claude-draft">Slot · Brydges Place, the back door of the Harp, and your old friend from the Green Sea, waiting. This time he sees you first.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘It was like a meeting in a side corridor of a mansion full of life.’</span>

<!-- Beat 1, he reads your night back: what you did with the ship. -->\
(if: $shipCall is "given")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · He knows you gave QUIET FRANKIE ASHTON’S name on the phone, and that you chose to.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘…the mind and the instincts of a burglar are of the same kind as the mind and the instincts of a police officer. Both recognise the same conventions…’</span>](else-if: $shipCall is "slipped")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · He knows ASHTON’S name came out of you on the phone, drunk, unchosen.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. III:</i> ‘There is no occupation that fails a man more completely than that of a secret agent of police.’</span>](else-if: $shipCall is "kept")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · He knows you hung up on QUIET FRANKIE and the Debt still stands.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘The mind of Chief Inspector Heat was inaccessible to ideas of revolt. But his thieves were not rebels.’</span>](else-if: $shipNews is "sunk")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You heard she went down off the Old Head of Kinsale. He knows more than the news did.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘Not accustomed, as the doctors are, to examine closely the mangled remains of human beings, he had been shocked by the sight disclosed to his view…’</span>](else-if: $shipNews is not "")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You have only heard the rumour of the ship. He knows it from the inside.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘A department does not know so much as some of its servants.’</span>](else:)[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You have heard nothing of the ship. He tells you about it.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. VI:</i> ‘There are things not fit for everybody to know.’</span>]

<!-- What you did in the cellar, if you gave COPPER a name. -->\
(if: $crossed is "red")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · He knows you gave COPPER RED’S name in the cellar.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. VI:</i> ‘Private friendship, private information, private use of it—that’s how I look upon it.’</span>

](else-if: $crossed is "john")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · He knows you gave COPPER JOHN’S name in the cellar.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. VI:</i> ‘Private friendship, private information, private use of it—that’s how I look upon it.’</span>

]\
<!-- The truth of the ship tonight, which he knows whether or not you do. -->\
(if: $shipFate is "afloat")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · Tonight the ship is still afloat. What he knows of that, or means to do about it.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. II:</i> ‘A bomb outrage to have any influence on public opinion now must go beyond the intention of vengeance or terrorism. It must be purely destructive.’</span>](else:)[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · Tonight the ship has gone down. What he knows of that.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘The complexion of that case had somehow forced upon him the general idea of the absurdity of things human…’</span>]

<span class="claude-draft">[[Hear him out|Harp Alley Ask]]</span>

:: Harp Alley Ask [outdoor] {"position":"300,1580","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Beat 2, the ask. HEAT's face: the law wants a name for the shipment. The names on offer are the ones you have come to know tonight: COPPER from the cellar door, QUIET FRANKIE and ASHTON from THE GREAT HAM's rumour or the phone, ST. JOHN from the Debt or the phone. "Nothing" is always there. A name given here does not count as the night's one crossing ($crossed is untouched) until Sam rules otherwise. -->
(set: $harpNamed to "")\
<span class="claude-draft">Slot · HEAT’S face: reasonable, official, the law speaking. He wants a name for the shipment.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. VI:</i> ‘When it comes to that I would deal with the devil himself, and take the consequences.’</span>

(if: $metSalvu is true)[<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Give him SALVU COPPER")[(set: $harpNamed to "copper")(go-to: "Harp Alley Answer")]</span>
](if: ($hamRumour is true) or ($shipNews is "asked") or ($ashtonSold is true))[<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Give him QUIET FRANKIE")[(set: $harpNamed to "frankie")(go-to: "Harp Alley Answer")]</span>
](if: ($hamRumour is true) or ($holdsAshtonName is true))[<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Give him ASHTON GRANGER")[(set: $harpNamed to "ashton")(go-to: "Harp Alley Answer")]</span>
](if: ($haunts contains $haunt4) or ($shipNews is "asked"))[<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Give him JOHN ST. JOHN")[(set: $harpNamed to "stjohn")(go-to: "Harp Alley Answer")]</span>
]<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Give him nothing")[(set: $harpNamed to "nothing")(go-to: "Harp Alley Answer")]</span>

:: Harp Alley Answer [outdoor] {"position":"300,1590","size":"100,100"}
<!-- The two faces answer you. Give a name and the PROFESSOR's contempt turns on you: you have joined the crooks' trade. Give nothing and HEAT marks you down. Neither is clean. -->
(if: $harpNamed is "nothing")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You give him nothing. HEAT’S face: he marks you down.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘Not yet. When I want you I will know where to find you.’</span>](else:)[(if: $harpNamed is "copper")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You give him SALVU COPPER.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘Thieving was not a sheer absurdity. It was a form of human industry, perverse indeed, but still an industry exercised in an industrious world…’</span>](else-if: $harpNamed is "frankie")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You give him QUIET FRANKIE.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘They were his fellow-citizens gone wrong because of imperfect education…’</span>](else-if: $harpNamed is "ashton")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You give him ASHTON GRANGER.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. II:</i> ‘Property seems to them an indestructible thing.’</span>](else-if: $harpNamed is "stjohn")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You give him JOHN ST. JOHN.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. IV:</i> ‘Revolution, legality—counter moves in the same game; forms of idleness at bottom identical.’</span>]

<span class="claude-draft">Slot · The PROFESSOR’S face: contempt. Crooks, crypto-bourgeois, and now you among them.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. IV:</i> ‘Like to like. The terrorist and the policeman both come from the same basket.’</span>]

<span class="claude-draft">[[His hand is in his pocket|Harp Alley Standoff]]</span>

:: Harp Alley Standoff [outdoor] {"position":"300,1600","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Beat 3, the hand in his pocket: whoever has less to lose wins. Push him and your state decides it. Wrecked (morale or sobriety under 30, the game's drunk line) you are the PROFESSOR, untouchable, and he walks away shaken, as HEAT does in Conrad. Otherwise you have something to lose and he has you. Let it lie and he leaves with the upper hand. The 30 is a dial. -->
<span class="claude-draft">Slot · His hand stays in his pocket. Whatever is in it, you don’t see.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. IV:</i> ‘I walk always with my right hand closed round the india-rubber ball which I have in my trouser pocket.’</span>

<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Push him")[(if: ($confidence < 30) or ($sobriety < 30))[(set: $harpOutcome to "untouchable")](else:)[(set: $harpOutcome to "held")](go-to: "Harp Alley End")]</span>
<span class="claude-draft">(link: "Let it lie")[(set: $harpOutcome to "backed")(go-to: "Harp Alley End")]</span>

:: Harp Alley End [outdoor] {"position":"300,1610","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Who walks away shaken. Stakes still to be decided by Sam; nothing here moves a meter yet. -->
(if: $harpOutcome is "untouchable")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You have nothing left to lose and he sees it. He is the one who walks away shaken.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘With all his healthy contempt for the spirit dictating such speeches, the atrocious allusiveness of the words had its effect on Chief Inspector Heat.’</span>](else-if: $harpOutcome is "held")[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You have too much to lose and he knows it. You walk away shaken.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘Life had such a strong hold upon him that a fresh wave of nausea broke out in slight perspiration upon his brow.’</span>](else:)[<span class="claude-draft">Slot · You let it lie. He goes back in through the Harp’s door with the upper hand.<br><i>Conrad, The Secret Agent, ch. V:</i> ‘You may be sure our side will win in the end.’</span>]

