:: Watkins [venue-cecilcourt] {"position":"300,1580","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam: "more interesting ... the words appearing not all at once or moving around"; his words unchanged): the window mists then fizzes clear letter by letter; the waltz paragraph sways in three-four, twice-heard; the last arrives a word to a beat, the two dancers in brass, still turning. A click shows it all; reduced motion shows it plain. (dssWatkinsVision) --><div class="wk-vision"><p class="wk-p wk-glass">First you see only yourself reflecting on the window; but let a moment pass, then things fizz down to clarity, like when the bubbles resolve on the tonic.</p><p class="wk-p wk-waltz">A waltz strikes up, twice-muffled, as if it came both from inside the bookshop and your own inner ear.</p><p class="wk-p wk-dance">You watch: from the stockroom, brassy figures emerge, lifesized and dancing; it is Madame Blavatsky, she is waltzing with the Beast.</p></div><div class="wk-links">
<!-- 2026-10-12 (the venues audit): the waltz once a night; after it, its own "Onward, then." straight to the shop (it replayed on every trip, the page's return included, and swung morale 14 each time) -->(if: $waltzDone is true)[[[Onward, then.|Approach O'Flatterly]]](else:)[[[Waltz on to the light|Cecil Court Waltz]]]
