(if: $hadChippy is true and $tookLily1 is false)[<span class="dss-flower-only-marker"></span>]
You find it after some looking, where you always knew it was: the Chinese Fish and Chips.

<!-- 2026-10-21 (ordering audit): LILY's name waits for Night Ahead Part Two, as her phone rings do in every venue; before it the lily is here unnamed, as in the other rooms -->(if: ($tookLily1 is not true) and ($lilyNamed is true))[You’re eating at the counter when somebody passes the window: that’s LILY.]

(if: $tookLily1 is false)[|lily1>[(display: "Lily SVG")]\
(click-replace: ?lily1)[(if: $sobriety < 30)[(display: "Lily SVG")(unless: $lostToDrink contains "lily1")[(set: $lostToDrink to $lostToDrink + (a: "lily1"))]<span class="lily-glimpse lily-fade">She was leaving town the day after PIERS GAV. She found you and your mates in a pub garden; you hadn’t slept and the acid was still funny. This is the flower you tried to give her. The one you picked in the ha-ha of some big house and kept in your buttonhole all night, and which she wouldn’t take.</span>](else:)[(set: $lostToDrink to $lostToDrink - (a: "lily1"))(set: $lilyCount to $lilyCount + 1)(set: $tookLily1 to true)(display: "Next Redraw")<span class="dss-lily-count" style="display:none">(print: $lilyCount)</span>(display: "Lily SVG")<span class="lily-glimpse lily-fade">That must be her, as tall as the Amazon; her joints articulate how you remember.</span>(if: $lilyHintShown is false)[(set: $lilyHintShown to true)<div class="lily-glimpse-hint">Gather flowers. There are five to find.</div>](if: $lilyCount is 5)[(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 25))(set: $sobriety to ($statGain: $sobriety, 15))<div class="pent-reveal-note"><div class="pent-reveal-title">⛤ THE PENTACLE ⛤</div><div class="pent-reveal-body">Five flowers, five points; the city draws its star around you.</div><span class="inventory-note">MORALE +25 | SOBRIETY +15</span></div><script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssRevealPentangleOnMap)window.dssRevealPentangleOnMap();},900);</script>]]]](else:)[<div class="lily-taken">(display: "Lily SVG")</div>]

