:: Copper Word Accepted [venue-cellar] {"position":"2100,500","size":"100,100"}
(set: $awaitingCopperPwd to false)(set: $gaveCopperWord to true)<!-- 2026-10-17 (played live): the words were said; Fight Victory keys COPPER's acceptance on this, not on knowing them -->\
<div class="cellar-scene">
<div class="cellar-light"></div>
You say the words you were given. COPPER’S eyebrows freeze as they are rising, and in the throttling of momentum seem to rise above themselves, like ghosts, in placid supplication. Then his masseters, their wreck-head sneer, become again the tyrants in his visage.

‘I see. We’ll have it soft then. But you still knocked on my door, lad.’

He’s closer. QUIET FRANKIE won’t look up but ASHTON GRANGER has; she stops doodling.

[[Brace yourself|Fight starts]]
</div>

:: Copper confronts [venue-cellar char-salvu] {"position":"1800,700","size":"100,100"}
(set: $awaitingCopperPwd to false)\
<!-- Swinging bulb -->
<div class="cellar-bulb-wrap">
<svg width="48" height="90" viewBox="0 0 48 90"><!-- Wire from ceiling --><line x1="24" y1="0" x2="24" y2="30" stroke="#888878" stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.75"/><!-- Socket cap --><rect x="17" y="28" width="14" height="10" rx="2.5"fill="rgba(80,78,65,0.9)" stroke="rgba(160,155,120,0.7)" stroke-width="1"/><!-- Socket ring detail --><rect x="19" y="36" width="10" height="3" rx="1"fill="none" stroke="rgba(150,145,110,0.55)" stroke-width="0.8"/><!-- Outer glow halo --><ellipse cx="24" cy="60" rx="20" ry="22"fill="rgba(255,245,160,0.12)"/><!-- Bulb body — pear shape, bright and solid --><path d="M24,38 C16,38 10,45 10,55 C10,67 16,78 24,78 C32,78 38,67 38,55 C38,45 32,38 24,38 Z"fill="rgba(255,252,210,0.95)" stroke="rgba(220,210,160,0.6)" stroke-width="0.8"/><!-- Inner warm core --><ellipse cx="24" cy="57" rx="9" ry="11"fill="rgba(255,240,120,0.55)"/><!-- Filament — W-shape --><path d="M18,60 L20,53 L24,58 L28,53 L30,60"fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,200,40,0.95)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/><!-- Neck base ring --><rect x="20" y="75" width="8" height="3" rx="1"fill="rgba(200,195,155,0.65)" stroke="none"/></svg>
</div>
<div class="cellar-scene">
<div class="cellar-light"></div>
COPPER gets closer.

‘I asked you a question,’ he says.

[[Brace yourself|Fight starts]]
[[Stand your ground|Stand your ground]]
</div>

:: Alba Complete [piano-bed] {"position":"1550,50","size":"100,100"}
<span id="dss-end-complete" hidden></span><script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssEndgameStage)window.dssEndgameStage("complete",document.getElementById("dss-end-complete"));},0);</script>\
<script>(function(){/* HTTP-prefetch the iframe HTML and the vendored THREE.js script. Avoiding a hidden iframe here because Chrome throttles script execution in off-screen iframes — Three.js inits but the scene-build script never runs, and we land on Dawn Approach with an empty canvas. Plain fetch puts the HTML in the cache; the THREE library link-preload primes the network so the fresh iframe on Dawn Approach mounts fast. */try{fetch('oxford-street-from-centre-point-3d-static.html',{cache:'force-cache'});}catch(e){}if(!document.getElementById('dss-three-prefetch')){var l=document.createElement('link');l.id='dss-three-prefetch';l.rel='preload';l.as='script';l.href='vendor/three/three.min.js';document.head.appendChild(l);}})();</script>\
(if: $aoifeRework)[<!-- A3 — the family flashes up as a brief modal "vision" over the dawn screen,
     holds ~1.5s, then dissolves to reveal the ending text. Fixed overlay driven by a
     CSS keyframe; pointer-events:none so it never blocks "Traveller, wake!". -->
<div class="a3-flash"><div class="memory-photo memory-aoife memory-photo-a3"><div class="mp-image"><svg class="mp-bg" viewBox="0 0 300 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"><defs><radialGradient id="aoifeA3" cx="50%" cy="34%" r="86%"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#bcd0e8" stop-opacity="0.85"/><stop offset="30%" stop-color="#6a84b0" stop-opacity="0.46"/><stop offset="62%" stop-color="#28365a" stop-opacity="0.30"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0a1020" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient></defs><rect width="300" height="200" fill="url(#aoifeA3)"/></svg><div class="mp-prose">There’s a whole remembered life still in the future, with your daughter and AOIFE.</div></div></div></div>
]\
<div class="ending-pane">London is all before you: Tyburn, Bloomsbury, Fitzrovia; St. Giles, at your feet; and Soho, which has dulled your soul and dressed you for the sun, in midnight’s cloak, throbs low and still, through its bruised capillaries.

You found the poem, the path to dawn’s bleak Albion.

[[Traveller, wake!|Dawn Approach White]]</div>

:: The Fetch {"position":"1600,50","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-13 (Sam): meeting the Fetch, TRISHA'S cat leaves you; she is on her step again -->(set: $catFollows to false)\
<!-- THE WEIGHTING (Sam, 2026-10-12: "the game is winnable too quickly ... without really engaging at all with the lily
     flowers or the haunts"). He opens the way on only to a night that has been lived: $needLilies of LILY's flowers and
     $needHaunts haunts (3 and 6, set in StoryInit and Start; tune them there). Before that he is a glimpse: no "Follow
     him", the count of what is still owed, and back to the night; a glimpse is not one of his two meetings. The night's
     forced ends still go through as before: the Coach fire, the Sanctum, "Give up. Sleep here.", "Lose" (No more) and
     the second blackout's road to the dawn. -->\
(unless: $needLilies is a number)[(set: $needLilies to 3)](unless: $needHaunts is a number)[(set: $needHaunts to 6)]\
(set: _from to "")(if: (history:)'s length > 0)[(set: _from to (history:)'s last)]\
(set: _forced to ($coachBurnt is true or $sanctumDone is true or $blackouts >= 2 or _from is "Coach and Horses lock" or _from is "No more" or _from is "The Sanctum" or _from is "The Coach Burns"))\
(set: _ready to (_forced or ($lilyCount >= $needLilies and $haunts's length >= $needHaunts)))\
<!-- 2026-10-11 (Sam, option C): at most two meetings with the Fetch a night; the second is final (no way back to the night). -->(if: _ready)[(set: $fetchMet to (cond: $fetchMet is a number, $fetchMet + 1, 1))]\
<!-- 2026-10-11 (Sam, B): the second meeting, he is already there: the walk is skipped and he stands close when you arrive. -->(if: $fetchMet >= 2 or ((not _ready) and $fetchGlimpsed is true))[<span id="dss-fetch-again" hidden></span>](if: not _ready)[(set: $fetchGlimpsed to true)]<!-- 2026-10-12: after the first glimpse he is already there too; the 15 s walk once is enough -->\
<span id="dss-end-fetch" hidden></span><script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssEndgameStage)window.dssEndgameStage("fetch",document.getElementById("dss-end-fetch"));},0);</script>\
<script>if (window.dssAudio && window.dssAudio.prewarmBed) window.dssAudio.prewarmBed('piano-eoin');setTimeout(function(){ if (window.dssAudio) window.dssAudio.uncannyBreath(); }, 400);</script>\
<script>(function(){/* Earliest practical prefetch of the Oxford-Street iframe HTML + the Three.js CDN script. Fires here (The Fetch → Approach Centre Point → Alba Complete/Incomplete → Dawn Approach), so HTTP cache has the assets long before the iframe mounts. The later prefetch passages keep the same calls for safety; all are idempotent (HTTP cache dedup + id check on the link element). Hidden-iframe preload was ruled out previously because Chrome throttles scripts in non-visible frames. */try{fetch('oxford-street-from-centre-point-3d-static.html',{cache:'force-cache'});}catch(e){}if(!document.getElementById('dss-three-prefetch')){var l=document.createElement('link');l.id='dss-three-prefetch';l.rel='preload';l.as='script';l.href='vendor/three/three.min.js';document.head.appendChild(l);}})();</script>\
<div class="glass-pane">(display: "Fetch Street SVG")<div id="fetch-reveal" style="display:none">

<!-- 2026-10-24 sweep: THE CROWN came on a glimpse too (played live: 11 haunts, 2 flowers, "Not yet" showing, and the twelfth haunt landed with it, turning the header to OPUS/STATE before the night was lived); a glimpse is not a meeting, so the crown waits for one -->(if: _ready and $haunts's length >= 11 and not ($haunts contains $haunt12))[
(set: $haunts to $haunts + (a: $haunt12))
<div class="haunt-box">
<div class="haunt-header">⟡ HAUNT COLLECTED ⟡</div>
<div class="haunt-name">THE CROWN</div>
<div class="haunt-description">From Kether to Malkuth and back again.</div>
<div class="haunt-work"><em>The work: Exaltatio.</em></div>
<div class="haunt-progress">(print: $haunts's length) of 12 caught</div>(display: "Mantra Syllable Cue")
</div>

]\
<!-- 2026-10-11 (Sam, A): the second meeting, his Beckett line above the way on. 2026-10-12 (Sam): the first meeting has his Baudelaire, by way of Eliot, in the same place. -->(if: _ready and $fetchMet >= 2)[<div style="margin:0 0 0.9em;font-style:italic;">‘I can’t go on, I’ll go on.’</div>](else:)[<div style="margin:0 0 0.9em;font-style:italic;">‘You! hypocrite lecteur! – mon semblable, – mon frère!’</div>](if: _ready)[[[Follow him|Approach Centre Point]]]
(if: not _ready)[There are still flowers to gather in the night, and work yet to be done.
<div class="fetch-owed"><!-- 2026-10-21 (ordering audit): the tally names LILY only once Night Ahead Part Two has -->(if: $lilyNamed is true)[LILY’S FLOWERS](else:)[FLOWERS] (print: $lilyCount) of (print: $needLilies) · HAUNTS (print: $haunts's length) of (print: $needHaunts)</div>](else-if: not ($sanctumDone is true or $coachBurnt is true or $fetchMet >= 2))[(if: $lilyCount < 5 or $haunts's length < 12)[
You can leave now, perhaps it’s wise to get out. But there are still flowers to gather in the night, and work yet to be done.]]
(unless: _ready and ($sanctumDone is true or $coachBurnt is true or $fetchMet >= 2))[

<span class="back-to-night-glow">[[Not yet. Back to the night.|Dean Street]]</span>]</div></div><script>(function(){var el=document.getElementById('fetch-reveal');var still=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;var again=!!document.getElementById('dss-fetch-again');if(still){var sv=document.querySelector('svg.fetch-street');if(sv&&sv.pauseAnimations){sv.pauseAnimations();sv.setCurrentTime(21);}}else if(again){var sv2=document.querySelector('svg.fetch-street');if(sv2&&sv2.setCurrentTime)sv2.setCurrentTime(7.2);}var shown=false;function show(){if(shown||!el||!document.body.contains(el))return;shown=true;document.removeEventListener('pointerdown',skip,true);document.removeEventListener('keydown',skip,true);el.style.opacity='0';el.style.display='';el.style.transition='opacity 1.4s ease';requestAnimationFrame(function(){requestAnimationFrame(function(){el.style.opacity='1';});});}function skip(ev){if(!el||!document.body.contains(el)){document.removeEventListener('pointerdown',skip,true);document.removeEventListener('keydown',skip,true);return;}if(ev.type==='keydown'&&ev.key!==' '&&ev.key!=='Enter')return;if(ev.target&&ev.target.closest&&ev.target.closest('tw-link,button,a,.stat-bars,#stat-bars-lifted,tw-header'))return;var sv3=document.querySelector('svg.fetch-street');if(sv3&&sv3.setCurrentTime)sv3.setCurrentTime(21);show();}document.addEventListener('pointerdown',skip,true);document.addEventListener('keydown',skip,true);/* 2026-10-29 nightwork (smoothness): the 15 s walk could not be hurried; a click, Space or Enter now ends it and shows the way on, as the typewriter pages do */setTimeout(show,still?400:(again?7800:15000));})()</script>

