]\
<!-- Keep useful key venues reachable after their ordinary business is finished. -->\
(if: $coachUrgent is false and $inisToldOfPillars is true)[\
(if: $keySlip is "seed")[[[The Coach and Horses|Approach The Coach]]]
(if: $keyTicket is "seed")[[[The Halibut (Fish and Chips)|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]]
(if: $keyCocaine is "seed" and $hasTrishaMatchbook is true)[[[Trisha’s|Approach Trisha's]]]<!-- 2026-10-11 structure pass 3: Trisha's opens as a key door only once the matchbook has told you where it is; before, the door lit up the moment INIS named the pillar, ahead of LACKLAND's back room. -->
]\
<!-- The old Voice shortcut stays removed. The way out is no longer a line of
     text here: it is the north-edge tile on the map, towards Centre Point, and
     the link that opens it is parked off-screen above. It is always available
     but never advertised (Sam, 2026-09-13: "I don't want them to know about head
     towards the dawn... it's mad to tell them how to quit the game from the very
     start"). Discovery only. Towards Dawn does the warning once they get there. -->\
(if: $coachUrgent is false and $hadChippy is true and $tookLily1 is false)[<div class="choice-box">[[Back to the chippy|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]</div> <span class="lp">❁</span>](else-if: $coachUrgent is false and $hadChippy is true)[<span class="greyed-out">The Halibut (Fish and Chips)</span> <span class="lp lp-done">❀</span>
]\
(if: $coachUrgent is false and $confidence <= 5)[[[Give up on the night|No more]]
]\
]

:: Dido [dream pyre] {"position":"100,1700","size":"100,100"}
(unless: $visitedPyre is a boolean)[(set: $visitedPyre to false)]\
(set: $visitedPyre to true)\
<svg class="carthage-pyre" viewBox="0 0 500 95" width="100%" height="95" preserveAspectRatio="none"><defs><radialGradient id="cpGlow" cx="50%" cy="88%" r="72%"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#ffa040" stop-opacity="0.55"/><stop offset="18%" stop-color="#d4600a" stop-opacity="0.32"/><stop offset="55%" stop-color="#401808" stop-opacity="0.12"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient><radialGradient id="cpFlameCore" cx="50%" cy="80%" r="60%"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#fff0d0" stop-opacity="0.85"/><stop offset="35%" stop-color="#ffc868" stop-opacity="0.55"/><stop offset="70%" stop-color="#e88020" stop-opacity="0.30"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#c84808" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient><linearGradient id="cpTopFade" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="1"/><stop offset="35%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="0.6"/><stop offset="60%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="0"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="cpFade" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="1"/><stop offset="8%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="0"/><stop offset="92%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="0"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0a0a12" stop-opacity="1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="cpGround" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#3a2010" stop-opacity="0.5"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#1a0a08" stop-opacity="0.3"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="cpLogDark" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#3a1a08"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#140804"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="cpLogGlow" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#502410"/><stop offset="55%" stop-color="#c84808" stop-opacity="0.85"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#3a1808"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="cpShroud" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#2a1208"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0a0402"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="cpColumn" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#7a5a3a"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#3a2818"/></linearGradient></defs><g filter="url(#dss-ink)"><!-- Warm glow over the scene --><rect x="0" y="0" width="500" height="95" fill="url(#cpGlow)"/><!-- Ground --><rect x="0" y="80" width="500" height="15" fill="url(#cpGround)"/><!-- Distant ruin shapes on the horizon --><path d="M140,80 L142,55 L145,58 L148,52 L152,60 L156,55 L159,80 Z" fill="#2a1810" opacity="0.55"/><path d="M338,80 L341,48 L347,53 L351,46 L355,56 L359,50 L362,80 Z" fill="#2a1810" opacity="0.5"/><path d="M168,80 L171,68 L177,72 L180,80 Z" fill="#2a1810" opacity="0.42"/><path d="M324,80 L327,71 L332,75 L336,80 Z" fill="#2a1810" opacity="0.42"/><!-- Far-left broken column with fluting --><g opacity="0.7"><rect x="78" y="32" width="6" height="48" fill="url(#cpColumn)"/><line x1="79.5" y1="34" x2="79.5" y2="78" stroke="#1a0e06" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="81" y1="34" x2="81" y2="78" stroke="#1a0e06" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="82.5" y1="34" x2="82.5" y2="78" stroke="#1a0e06" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.55"/><rect x="76" y="29" width="10" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#806858"/><path d="M76,32 L86,29 L86,33 L76,36 Z" fill="#806858" opacity="0.6"/><!-- Fallen drum next to base --><ellipse cx="73" cy="80" rx="8" ry="2" fill="#3a2818" opacity="0.5"/><rect x="67" y="77" width="12" height="3.5" rx="0.5" fill="#806858" opacity="0.5"/><circle cx="69" cy="78.5" r="1.5" fill="#3a2010" opacity="0.65"/></g><!-- Far-right column — taller, slightly more eroded --><g opacity="0.65"><rect x="402" y="22" width="6" height="58" fill="url(#cpColumn)"/><line x1="403.5" y1="25" x2="403.5" y2="78" stroke="#1a0e06" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="405" y1="25" x2="405" y2="78" stroke="#1a0e06" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="406.5" y1="25" x2="406.5" y2="78" stroke="#1a0e06" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.55"/><rect x="400" y="19" width="10" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#806858"/><!-- Crack running down --><path d="M404,38 Q406,46 404,54 Q406,62 404,70" fill="none" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.55"/><!-- Lichen patch --><ellipse cx="407" cy="50" rx="1.8" ry="3.5" fill="#3a4828" opacity="0.4"/><!-- Rubble at base --><ellipse cx="416" cy="80" rx="10" ry="2.5" fill="#3a2818" opacity="0.45"/><rect x="408" y="76" width="8" height="4" rx="0.5" fill="#806858" opacity="0.5"/><circle cx="420" cy="79" r="1.7" fill="#3a2010" opacity="0.6"/></g><!-- ============================================================ --><!--   THE PYRE — built up of charred logs, body shrouded on top      --><!-- ============================================================ --><!-- Shadow on ground --><ellipse cx="250" cy="82" rx="72" ry="3.5" fill="#0a0402" opacity="0.65"/><!-- Bottom log course (long, dark, charred) --><rect x="190" y="74" width="120" height="6" rx="1.5" fill="url(#cpLogDark)"/><rect x="190" y="74" width="120" height="2" fill="#5a2010" opacity="0.55"/><!-- Log end-grain on each end --><circle cx="192" cy="77" r="2.6" fill="#3a1408"/><circle cx="192" cy="77" r="1.6" fill="#0a0402"/><circle cx="308" cy="77" r="2.6" fill="#3a1408"/><circle cx="308" cy="77" r="1.6" fill="#0a0402"/><!-- Cross-grain split lines --><line x1="210" y1="74" x2="210" y2="80" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.6"/><line x1="232" y1="74" x2="232" y2="80" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="252" y1="74" x2="252" y2="80" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.6"/><line x1="270" y1="74" x2="270" y2="80" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="288" y1="74" x2="288" y2="80" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.6"/><!-- Second course (perpendicular, inset) --><rect x="202" y="68" width="96" height="6" rx="1" fill="url(#cpLogDark)"/><rect x="202" y="68" width="96" height="2" fill="#5a2010" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="220" y1="68" x2="220" y2="74" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="245" y1="68" x2="245" y2="74" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="275" y1="68" x2="275" y2="74" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.55"/><!-- Third course (top course, glowing — body rests on this) --><rect x="212" y="62" width="76" height="6" rx="1" fill="url(#cpLogGlow)"/><rect x="212" y="62" width="76" height="1.5" fill="#3a1408" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="232" y1="62" x2="232" y2="68" stroke="#1a0a04" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.65"/><line x1="252" y1="62" x2="252" y2="68" stroke="#1a0a04" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.65"/><line x1="270" y1="62" x2="270" y2="68" stroke="#1a0a04" stroke-width="0.4" opacity="0.65"/><!-- Glowing embers visible between top logs --><ellipse cx="240" cy="68.5" rx="3" ry="0.8" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.85"/><ellipse cx="262" cy="68.5" rx="2.4" ry="0.7" fill="#ffa040" opacity="0.8"/><ellipse cx="252" cy="68.5" rx="1.5" ry="0.6" fill="#fff0c0" opacity="0.7"/><!-- ────────────  BODY — shrouded, lying on the top course ──────────── --><!-- Main shroud body (lying horizontal across the logs) --><path d="M210,62 Q210,56 215,55 L285,55 Q290,56 290,62 Z" fill="url(#cpShroud)"/><!-- Body subtle shadow folds --><path d="M222,57 Q226,59 234,56 Q244,59 254,56 Q264,59 274,56 Q280,59 285,57" fill="none" stroke="#3a1810" stroke-width="0.7" opacity="0.55"/><!-- Head (left end, slightly raised) --><ellipse cx="212" cy="55" rx="6" ry="4.5" fill="#1a0a04"/><ellipse cx="211" cy="54" rx="2" ry="1.5" fill="#3a1810" opacity="0.6"/><!-- Foot end --><ellipse cx="288" cy="56" rx="4" ry="3.2" fill="#1a0a04"/><!-- Funeral cloth at the top edge — darker line --><line x1="208" y1="55" x2="290" y2="55" stroke="#0a0402" stroke-width="0.6" opacity="0.85"/><!-- ────────────  FLAMES — layered, rising around body ──────────── --><!-- Outer flame envelope (broad soft glow) --><ellipse cx="250" cy="46" rx="44" ry="38" fill="url(#cpFlameCore)" opacity="0.85"/><!-- Layer 1 — deep red outer --><path d="M208,62 Q198,40 218,16 Q224,28 230,4 Q236,22 242,2 Q248,22 252,1 Q256,22 262,3 Q268,22 274,8 Q280,28 286,16 Q300,38 292,62Z" fill="#8a2800" opacity="0.62"/><!-- Layer 2 — bright orange mid --><path d="M216,62 Q208,42 224,20 Q232,32 240,10 Q245,26 250,5 Q256,26 261,10 Q267,32 274,18 Q284,36 280,62Z" fill="#c04808" opacity="0.72"/><!-- Layer 3 — orange brighter --><path d="M224,62 Q220,44 232,26 Q238,36 244,14 Q248,28 252,10 Q257,28 262,14 Q268,32 275,28 Q282,46 272,62Z" fill="#d4600a" opacity="0.78"/><!-- Layer 4 — yellow inner --><path d="M232,62 Q228,46 238,30 Q242,40 246,20 Q250,30 254,18 Q258,30 262,22 Q268,38 266,62Z" fill="#e88020" opacity="0.75"/><!-- Layer 5 — bright yellow tongue --><path d="M238,62 Q237,48 242,34 Q246,40 250,28 Q254,40 257,28 Q260,42 261,62Z" fill="#ffa040" opacity="0.68"/><!-- Layer 6 — white-hot core --><path d="M244,62 Q243,50 248,38 Q250,46 252,38 Q254,46 256,62Z" fill="#ffc868" opacity="0.62"/><!-- White-hot tip --><ellipse cx="251" cy="42" rx="2.5" ry="5.5" fill="#fff0d0" opacity="0.55"/><!-- Side wisps (left and right) --><path d="M204,62 Q198,52 205,38 Q208,48 213,52 Q210,58 214,62Z" fill="#8a2800" opacity="0.45"/><path d="M296,62 Q302,52 295,38 Q292,48 287,52 Q290,58 286,62Z" fill="#8a2800" opacity="0.45"/><!-- Small lick on far left --><path d="M212,62 Q207,55 211,46 Q214,52 215,62Z" fill="#c04808" opacity="0.5"/><path d="M288,62 Q293,55 289,46 Q286,52 285,62Z" fill="#c04808" opacity="0.5"/><!-- ────────────  RISING EMBERS — many, varied glowing sparks ──────────── --><circle cx="245" cy="6" r="1.2" fill="#ffc868" opacity="0.9"/><circle cx="245" cy="6" r="0.5" fill="#fff0d0" opacity="0.95"/><circle cx="260" cy="9" r="0.9" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.85"/><circle cx="238" cy="11" r="1" fill="#ffa040" opacity="0.85"/><circle cx="268" cy="3" r="0.65" fill="#ffc868" opacity="0.85"/><circle cx="252" cy="2" r="0.75" fill="#fff0d0" opacity="0.9"/><circle cx="229" cy="7" r="0.7" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.8"/><circle cx="273" cy="13" r="1.1" fill="#ffa040" opacity="0.85"/><circle cx="242" cy="18" r="0.6" fill="#ffc868" opacity="0.8"/><circle cx="257" cy="16" r="0.55" fill="#ff6020" opacity="0.8"/><circle cx="223" cy="14" r="0.45" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.7"/><circle cx="278" cy="20" r="0.75" fill="#ffc868" opacity="0.8"/><circle cx="217" cy="22" r="0.55" fill="#ffa040" opacity="0.7"/><circle cx="285" cy="27" r="0.5" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.65"/><circle cx="248" cy="22" r="0.45" fill="#fff0d0" opacity="0.8"/><circle cx="234" cy="29" r="0.55" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.6"/><circle cx="266" cy="29" r="0.45" fill="#ffc868" opacity="0.6"/><circle cx="226" cy="35" r="0.35" fill="#d4600a" opacity="0.55"/><circle cx="276" cy="35" r="0.4" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.55"/><!-- ────────────  SMOKE WISPS — drift up off the highest flames ──────────── --><path d="M248,2 Q252,-3 246,-9" fill="none" stroke="#3a2a22" stroke-width="2.2" opacity="0.4" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M253,4 Q258,-2 251,-12" fill="none" stroke="#3a2a22" stroke-width="1.7" opacity="0.35" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M255,8 Q263,2 260,-7" fill="none" stroke="#3a2a22" stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.3" stroke-linecap="round"/><!-- ────────────  GROUND EMBERS — small glowing dots on the ground around the pyre ──────────── --><circle cx="180" cy="83" r="0.8" fill="#d4600a" opacity="0.45"/><circle cx="320" cy="81" r="0.6" fill="#c84a08" opacity="0.4"/><circle cx="200" cy="84" r="0.4" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.35"/><circle cx="305" cy="83" r="0.7" fill="#d4600a" opacity="0.45"/><circle cx="225" cy="85" r="0.35" fill="#ff8020" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="275" cy="84" r="0.45" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.35"/><circle cx="160" cy="84" r="0.5" fill="#ff8020" opacity="0.25"/><circle cx="340" cy="83" r="0.7" fill="#d4600a" opacity="0.3"/><circle cx="195" cy="82" r="0.3" fill="#ffa040" opacity="0.4"/><circle cx="313" cy="84" r="0.4" fill="#ff8030" opacity="0.35"/><!-- Edge fades to blend with surrounding prose --><rect x="0" y="0" width="500" height="95" fill="url(#cpTopFade)"/><rect x="0" y="0" width="500" height="95" fill="url(#cpFade)"/></g></svg>

On the pyre, DIDO is burning where she has burnt for 2,000 years.

The scent of her sour embers means something about lily of the valley.

(if: $hasMissingPage is false and $returnedPage is false)[‘Stay,’ she says, ‘My Carthage is meant for you. She is in her valley and will not return. Rest here and think no more about England.’]\
(else:)[‘You’re back,’ she says. ‘Carthage was always meant for you. What you took from the fire is yours; there is nothing else here. She is in her valley. Lie down beside me, now.’]

(link: "⟡ LORE: Her Dying Words ⟡")[(set: _lore to "Her Dying Words")(display: "Lore Read")<div class="dido-words"><span class="latin">Littora littoribus contraria, fluctibus undas<br>
Imprecor: arma armis: pugnent ipsique nepotes:<br>
Liue false Æneas, truest Dido dyes,<br>
Sic sic iuuat ire sub umbras.</span>
<hr class="didoRule">
<span class="english">Shores against shores; waves, waves;<br>
I curse, arms against arms, you and your children.<br>
Live false Aeneas, truest Dido dies,<br>
So, so happily I go, under shades.</span></div>]

(if: $knowsAboutPage is true and $hasMissingPage is false)[[[Reach into the flames|Rescue the page]]]

(set: _carthageDone to ((history:) contains "LINE 2") and ($hasMissingPage is true or $returnedPage is true))\
(if: _carthageDone)[\
The fire must burn with you or without you.

<span class="guided-link">[[Rest here|Stay in Carthage]]</span>
](else-if: $hasMissingPage is true or $returnedPage is true)[<span class="guided-link">[[Rest here|Stay in Carthage]]</span>]
(else:)[

(if: $confidence <= 15)[[[Return to the shore|The coast of Carthage]]](else:)[(if: $haunts's length >= 3)[[[Go back to shore|Carthage shore]]]]

(unless: $knowsAboutPage is true and $hasMissingPage is false)[[[Rest here|Stay in Carthage]]]]

:: Entering The Pillars of Hercules [venue-pillars] {"position":"300,1100","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-17 (design note 5.5): a reader cannot read a book that is not in the bag (left, fenced, sold or lent) -->(set: _bagBook to ((($bookAt is not a string) or ($bookAt is "")) and ($bookSold is not true) and (($bookLent is not a string) or ($bookLent is ""))))\
<!-- Sam, 2026-09-14: "you can return to the Pillars again soon and get three
     phone calls very quickly". Before the critic, the pub holds the Aoife call
     and the Ham and nothing else — the Lily rings wait for the French or the
     Coach, so bouncing in and out cannot farm them. -->
(set: _pillarsOpen to ($metCritic is true))\
(set: _lilyRing to (_pillarsOpen and ($ringSnoozed is not true) and ($lilyNamed is true) and ($lilyCount >= 2) and ($hadLilyCall1 is false) and ($hadPhoneCall is true) and (($returns - $phoneCallReturnsAt) >= 3) and ($visited contains "Pillars") and ($visited's Pillars is true)))<!-- 2026-10-24 sweep: every comparison bracketed; Harlowe read the long unbracketed chain as true with $ringSnoozed true (tested in a scratch build), so a refused ring came straight back on "Back to the bar" -->\
(set: _dualRing to (_pillarsOpen and ($refusedDualRing is not true) and ($lilyCount >= 2) and ($hadLilyCall1 is true) and ($hadDualRing is false) and ($crossedThreshold is true) and (($returns - $lilyCall1ReturnsAt) >= 2) and ($visited contains "Pillars") and ($visited's Pillars is true)))\
<div id="pi-container"></div>\
<div class="pillars-scene">
(if: $inisToldOfPillars is true and $dreamKey is not "")[<svg class="pillar centre" viewBox="0 0 34 280" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet"><defs><linearGradient id="pf3" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#f0d090" stop-opacity="0.98"/><stop offset="50%" stop-color="#d4ae6a" stop-opacity="0.85"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#a08648" stop-opacity="0.45"/></linearGradient><radialGradient id="pf3glow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="55%"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#f5d490" stop-opacity="0.55"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#f5d490" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient></defs><ellipse cx="17" cy="140" rx="40" ry="180" fill="url(#pf3glow)"/><rect x="1" y="252" width="32" height="8" fill="none" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="1.3"/><rect x="4" y="246" width="26" height="7" fill="none" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="1.2"/><line x1="5" y1="246" x2="6" y2="20" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="1.3"/><line x1="29" y1="246" x2="28" y2="20" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="1.3"/><line x1="5.5" y1="44" x2="28.5" y2="44" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="66" x2="28.5" y2="66" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="88" x2="28.5" y2="88" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="110" x2="28.5" y2="110" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="132" x2="28.5" y2="132" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="154" x2="28.5" y2="154" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="176" x2="28.5" y2="176" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="198" x2="28.5" y2="198" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="220" x2="28.5" y2="220" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="5.5" y1="242" x2="28.5" y2="242" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="0.75"/><line x1="10" y1="20" x2="10" y2="245" stroke="#d4ae6a" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="14" y1="20" x2="14" y2="245" stroke="#d4ae6a" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="17" y1="20" x2="17" y2="245" stroke="#d4ae6a" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="20" y1="20" x2="20" y2="245" stroke="#d4ae6a" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><line x1="24" y1="20" x2="24" y2="245" stroke="#d4ae6a" stroke-width="0.35" opacity="0.5"/><path d="M6,20 Q5,10 3,4 L31,4 Q29,10 28,20" fill="none" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="1.3"/><rect x="1" y="0" width="32" height="5" fill="none" stroke="url(#pf3)" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg>(if: $sawThirdPillar is false)[<script>setTimeout(function(){var p=document.querySelector("tw-passage .pillar.centre");if(p)p.classList.add("first-sight");if(window.dssAudio&&window.dssAudio.loreUnravel){window.dssAudio.loreUnravel();}},150);</script>(set: $sawThirdPillar to true)]]
(unless: $visited is a datamap)[(set: $visited to (dm:))]\
(unless: $visited contains "Pillars")[(set: $visited's Pillars to false)]\
<!-- THE MATCHBOX (2026-10-12, Sam: back to the Pillars). The card says "On the way out", so the Pillars only marks it due and it shows as you step back onto Dean Street. -->
(if: $hasMatches is false and not ($inisToldOfPillars is true and $dreamKey is a string and ($dreamKey is not "") and ($pillarsNoAuto is not true) and $sobriety >= 30))[(set: $pillarsMatchesDue to true)]\
<!-- 2026-10-24 (Sam, Q10): the third pillar judged you after the pub's own toll, so a player told to sober up on the street walked in at 30 to 38, paid the entry and was turned away again; $pillarsToll is what this entry cost and the gate below forgives it (drinks inside still count) -->(unless: $pillarsToll is a number)[(set: $pillarsToll to 0)](if: $resumingFromCall is true)[(set: $resumingFromCall to false)](else:)[(set: $pillarsToll to $sobriety)(set: $sobriety to ($statLoss: $sobriety, 9))(set: $pillarsToll to $pillarsToll - $sobriety)\
(unless: $pillarsVisits is a num)[(set: $pillarsVisits to 0)](set: $pillarsVisits to $pillarsVisits + 1)\
(if: $visited's Pillars is false)[(set: $visited's Pillars to true)\
(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 12))]](display: "Bars Now")<!-- 2026-10-24 (Sam, Q1): the header drew the bars before this page's draw, so the STATS primer (Primer Footer, the first time a bar leaves 70) typed itself out beside bars still reading 70/70; the bars move on this page now -->\
<!-- AOIFE'S CALL is now a CHOICE (2026-07-22): the forced redirect is gone; the
     ring block in the body offers Accept / "I'm not here". $hadPhoneCall stays
     false on decline, so it rings again on every Pillars entry until answered.
     (Ordering note preserved: the first-visit block above still runs before any
     call, so $visited's Pillars and the +12 are safe.) -->
\
(unless: $justDranked is a boolean)[(set: $justDranked to false)]\
<!-- 2026-10-12 (the Pillars audit): his opening verse is the first entry's, as the French's entry prose is; it no longer comes back after every drink, every call and every visit -->(set: _pDrank to ($justDranked is true))\
(if: $justDranked is true)[(set: $justDranked to false)<span id="drink-type-data-pillars" style="display:none">(print: $lastDrink)</span><script>if(window.showDrinkPopupSafe){window.showDrinkPopupSafe(function(){var el=document.getElementById('drink-type-data-pillars');return (el&&el.textContent.trim())||'stout';},250);}else{setTimeout(function(){if(window.showDrinkPopup){var el=document.getElementById('drink-type-data-pillars');var t=(el&&el.textContent.trim())||'stout';window.showDrinkPopup(t);}},250);}</script>]\
(unless: $pillarsVerseShown is true or _pDrank)[(set: $pillarsVerseShown to true)If you cross the threshold of the Pillars you’ve already made your choice.

Whatever more you choose comes out in the wash:

<div class="verse">Hobson has supt, and ’s newly gon to bed.</div>\
]\
(unless: $worldsVisited is an array)[(set: $worldsVisited to (a:))](unless: $inisToldOfPillars is a boolean)[(set: $inisToldOfPillars to false)]\
(if: $inisToldOfPillars is true and $dreamKey is not "")[<div class="prose-tilde">~</div>]\
(display: "Key Guards")\
<!-- v2-expansion: third-pillar portal option. Fires when Inis has tipped
     the player off AND there is a pocket-key in hand.
     CHANGED 2026-09-12 (Sam: "the Pillars isn't open enough"). The old
     rule was a hard cap of two completed worlds a playthrough, which left
     three of the five keys unspendable and shut the column while the
     player was still collecting. The KEY is now the ticket: carrying one
     opens the column and the crossing spends it (the hidden world links
     in Third Pillar Portal do the spending), so a night self-limits at
     five crossings, because there are five keys and each is consumed by
     the crossing that uses it. (This note used to cite "one lap each out
     of sixteen" as a second limiter. That is gone: the night is open now
     and a crossing costs nothing. Key consumption still limits it alone.)
     The < 5 guard only
     stops the column opening onto an empty pool once every world is done;
     the portal's own fallback would otherwise dead-end there. -->\
<!-- Different unfinished worlds may be entered during the same night. -->\
<!-- STRAIGHT THROUGH (2026-09-14, Sam: "when you return to the pillars and have
     everything you need for a dream quest, it should immediately go to the third
     pillar screen when you walk in off the map"). $pillarsNoAuto is set by the
     portal's own turn-backs, so coming BACK from the column lands you in the pub
     instead of being thrown straight out to it again. Without that guard the two
     passages would bounce you between them for ever. -->\
(unless: $pillarsNoAuto is a boolean)[(set: $pillarsNoAuto to false)]\
(if: ($inisToldOfPillars is true) and ($dreamKey is not "") and ($pillarsNoAuto is false) and (($sobriety + $pillarsToll) >= 30))[(go-to: "Third Pillar Portal")]\
(set: $pillarsNoAuto to false)\
(if: $inisToldOfPillars is true and $dreamKey is not "")[
<div>
A third pillar rises. It is knit of the storm’s blue runoff and the Straits of Gibraltar; a third between the Pillars of Hercules.

The (print: $keyNames's ($dreamKey)) in your pocket seems to heat with some occulted energy.
</div>

(if: ($sobriety + $pillarsToll) < 30)[<div class="choice-box">[[Step into the third blue post|The Wall]]</div>](else:)[<div class="choice-box">[[Step into the third blue post|Third Pillar Portal]]</div>]
]\
<!-- 2026-10-06 (Dr Quill): "if you have no key or no word from Inis then you just shouldn't see the pillar at all".
     The shut-pillar paragraph is gone; the 2D and 3D pillar show only with Inis's word and a key, or when the synthesis is ready.
     His shut-pillar words, kept here: There is the third pillar, the one that Inis O’Flatterly told you about. For the moment it is shut. It wants paying and your pockets are empty. Find something small in the night to fund your passage. -->\
<!-- v2-expansion: the synthesis ritual link, revealed only when the
     player has earned all 5 world gifts across their lifetime
     (localStorage). The third pillar isn't a portal now — it's the
     site of a ritual. The visible/hidden toggle happens in JS at the
     bottom of the passage. Gated on lifetime gifts only; a player
     can carry that knowledge into a fresh playthrough without having
     met Inis this run. -->\
<span id="dss-synth-visited" style="display:none">(print: $worldsVisited)</span><div id="dss-synthesis-link" style="display:none;">
<div class="prose-tilde">~</div>
<div>There is nothing more in the night for you to find.</div>

<div class="choice-box">[[Perform the synthesis|The Synthesis]]</div>
</div>\
<script>
(function(){
  try {
    var vis = document.getElementById('dss-synth-visited');
    var gifts = ((vis && vis.textContent) || '').split(',').map(function(x){ return x.trim(); }).filter(function(x){ return x; });
    if (gifts.length >= 5) { // 2026-10-09 structure pass: this night's five worlds, not the lifetime store
      var el = document.getElementById('dss-synthesis-link');
      if (el) el.style.display = 'block';
    }
  } catch(e) {}
})();
</script>\
(if: _lilyRing)[(set: $lilyCallReturn to "Entering The Pillars of Hercules")<div class="phone-ringing">A phone rings, the barman answers it, then looks you in the eye and mouths, ‘LILY’.

|lilyring>[(link: "Accept the call")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 6))(go-to: "Lily phone call 1")]
