(if: $refusedCalls is 2)[<div class="glass-pane">(display: "Fetch Window SVG")</div>]
[[Back to the bar|Entering The Pillars of Hercules]]]]]</div>]\
(else-if: _dualRing)[(set: $lilyCallReturn to "Entering The Pillars of Hercules")<div class="phone-ringing">The phone behind the bar rings.

|dualring>[(link: "Accept the call")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 7))(go-to: "The dual ring")]
(link: "Turn and leave")[(set: $refusedDualRing to true)(unless: $refusedCalls is a num)[(set: $refusedCalls to 0)](set: $refusedCalls to $refusedCalls + 1)(set: $resumingFromCall to true)(replace: ?dualring)[<!-- 2026-10-11 (Sam, option C part B): turning LILY away is a glimpse of the Fetch, not a meeting. PARKED (Sam): a musical intervention here, so the sound tells you something important has happened. --><div class="glass-pane">(display: "Fetch Window SVG")</div>
[[Back to the bar|Entering The Pillars of Hercules]]]]]</div>]\
(else:)[(if: $hadPhoneCall is true and $metCritic is true and $tookLily2 is false)[<span class="dss-flower-only-marker"></span>](if: $tookLily2 is false)[|lily2>[(display: "Lily SVG")]\
(click-replace: ?lily2)[(if: $sobriety < 30)[(display: "Lily SVG")(unless: $lostToDrink contains "lily2")[(set: $lostToDrink to $lostToDrink + (a: "lily2"))]<span class="lily-glimpse lily-fade">She was leaving town the day after PIERS GAV. She found you and your mates in a pub garden; you hadn’t slept and the acid was still funny. This is the flower you tried to give her. The one you picked in the ha-ha of some big house and kept in your buttonhole all night, and which she wouldn’t take.</span>](else:)[(set: $lostToDrink to $lostToDrink - (a: "lily2"))(set: $lilyCount to $lilyCount + 1)(set: $tookLily2 to true)(display: "Next Redraw")<span class="dss-lily-count" style="display:none">(print: $lilyCount)</span>(display: "Lily SVG")<span class="lily-glimpse lily-fade">There occurs, as you crossed the threshold of the Pillars, a sonic peculiarity seen elsewhere, for instance, in the acoustic mirrors on Dungeness. If you stand in that precise spot and the atmospherics are favourable, you might hear a noise made at that same instant anywhere in Soho. You hear her laugh.</span>(if: $lilyHintShown is false)[(set: $lilyHintShown to true)<div class="lily-glimpse-hint">Gather flowers. There are five to find.</div>](if: $lilyCount is 5)[(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 25))(set: $sobriety to ($statGain: $sobriety, 15))<div class="pent-reveal-note"><div class="pent-reveal-title">⛤ THE PENTACLE ⛤</div><div class="pent-reveal-body">Five flowers, five points; the city draws its star around you.</div><span class="inventory-note">MORALE +25 | SOBRIETY +15</span></div><script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssRevealPentangleOnMap)window.dssRevealPentangleOnMap();},900);</script>]]]](else:)[<div class="lily-taken">(display: "Lily SVG")</div>]
<!-- 2026-10-12 (the Pillars audit): AOIFE's ring no longer hides the Ham. Before the critic the pub holds the call AND the
     Ham (his 14 September rule), so both show, in any order; "no more business" waits until neither is left. --><!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam: want the book): AOIFE's call comes straight after the Ham refuses the book (in The critic's judgement); here it rings only on later visits, until answered -->(set: _aoifeRing to (($hadPhoneCall is false) and ($ringSnoozed is not true) and ($metCritic is true)))\
(if: _aoifeRing)[<div class="phone-ringing">Behind the bar a phone rings and your name is called.

|aoifering>[(link: "Accept the call")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 9))(go-to: "The phone call")]
(link: "I’m not here")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 4))(display: "Bars Now")(unless: $refusedCalls is a num)[(set: $refusedCalls to 0)](set: $refusedCalls to $refusedCalls + 1)(set: $ringSnoozed to true)(set: $resumingFromCall to true)(set: $refusedAoife to true)(replace: ?aoifering)[The barman looks you over utterly neutrally. He wishes he wasn’t paid to be part of this game. ‘Not seen him,’ he says, and puts back the receiver.
(if: $refusedCalls is 2)[<div class="glass-pane">(display: "Fetch Window SVG")</div>]
[[Back to the bar|Entering The Pillars of Hercules]]]]]</div>]\
(if: $metCritic is false)[Through the fumes, vapours and drink, you recognise a man.

<span class="lore-card-only">(link: "⟡ LORE: The Great Ham ⟡")[(set: _lore to "The Great Ham")(display: "Lore Read")<div class="lore-box">
<strong>⟡ THE GREAT HAM ⟡</strong>

<div class="editors-note">
<span class="editors-note-label">Editor’s note</span>
When Dr. Johnson, the harmless drudge and titan nonpareil among London’s literati in the mid-eighteenth century, was at the height of his powers, he was called the Great Cham. (Cham being a variant of Khan, that is: supreme leader).

When Ian Hamilton occupied a similar position, two centuries later, nobody (I am sadly but reliably informed) bestowed on him the obvious sobriquet. Here I intend to fix that.
</div>
</div>]</span>
(if: _bagBook)[[[Talk to the Great Ham|Talk to the critic]]]
<!-- 2026-10-03, Sam: the venue loops come in any order, so the bar and the crossing no longer wait for the critic (same links and gates as the branch below). -->
[[Get a drink at the bar|Which drink at the Pillars?]]
<!-- 2026-10-09, Sam: "get rid of the walk on water thing". The in-pub crossing is cut; the only road to Carthage is "Seek the shore" in the storm outside. -->
<!-- 2026-10-19 (Sam, playtest): no 'Not tonight.' on the opening words; the way out is the door, in the bar -->[[Back to the street|Dean Street]]]
(else-if: not _aoifeRing)[<!-- 2026-10-12: not under the third pillar, which is business -->(unless: (($inisToldOfPillars is true) and ($dreamKey is not "")) or ($tookLily2 is false))[You’ve no more business here.]<!-- 2026-10-21 (Sam): not while the lily is still there, which is business -->

(unless: $pillarsVisits is a num)[(set: $pillarsVisits to 0)]\
(if: $pillarsVisits >= 6)[‘Water, water everywhere. Another drop to drink.’]\
(else-if: $pillarsVisits >= 5)[Lamps are going out all over Soho. The light’s all in the sky now, its rare flickering. The flood’s unmapped these thin, mosaic streets.]\
(else-if: $pillarsVisits >= 3)[Outside, the flood is serious, hard to parse. Its spirit-levelling makes gravity loud and flattens everything beneath the still, phlegmatic sky.]\
(else:)[Outside, the weather’s looking worse. It wasn’t raining till you got inside, but now the runoff’s topped the kerb and is lapping at the threshold.]

[[Get a drink at the bar|Which drink at the Pillars?]]


[[Back to the street|Dean Street]]]]
</div>

</div>


:: Fetch Window SVG {"position":"1550,0","size":"100,100"}
<!-- The second-refusal glimpse: a leaded pub window (Pillars lattice language,
     spectral #8ac8dc) with the Fetch as a blurred dark shape behind it, pale
     lips mumbling on an irregular loop. Single flattened line + SMIL so it
     survives inside (replace:)/(if:) hooks (newlines would break the SVG). -->
<svg class="fetch-window" viewBox="0 0 300 286" width="100%" style="max-width:320px;display:block;margin:0.8em auto;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="At the window, a man with your face has stopped to stare in at you. He mouths, unmistakably: How many times do you want to pretend you aren't here?"><defs><filter id="fwBlurBig" x="-40%" y="-40%" width="180%" height="180%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="7"/></filter><filter id="fwBlurMid" x="-40%" y="-40%" width="180%" height="180%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="2.8"/></filter><filter id="fwBlurLip" x="-60%" y="-60%" width="220%" height="220%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="1.4"/></filter><radialGradient id="fwVig" cx="50%" cy="48%" r="70%"><stop offset="58%" stop-color="#000000" stop-opacity="0"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#000000" stop-opacity="0.35"/></radialGradient><linearGradient id="fwSheen" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0"/><stop offset="45%" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0.10"/><stop offset="55%" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0.03"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient><pattern id="fwLat" width="36" height="48" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M18,0 L36,24 L18,48 L0,24 Z" fill="none" stroke="#3f6b7d" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.8"/></pattern></defs><g filter="url(#dss-ink)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="300" height="200" fill="#bcc9cf"/><g><ellipse cx="70" cy="140" rx="110" ry="45" fill="#eef4f6" opacity="0.5" filter="url(#fwBlurBig)"><animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate" values="0 0; 42 -8; 0 0" dur="16s" repeatCount="indefinite"/></ellipse><ellipse cx="240" cy="55" rx="95" ry="38" fill="#e6eef1" opacity="0.45" filter="url(#fwBlurBig)"><animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate" values="0 0; -36 9; 0 0" dur="21s" repeatCount="indefinite"/></ellipse><ellipse cx="150" cy="185" rx="130" ry="35" fill="#f2f7f8" opacity="0.4" filter="url(#fwBlurB