:: Standing [venue-cellar] {"position":"2200,1350","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Swinging bulb -->
<div class="cellar-bulb-wrap">
<svg width="48" height="90" viewBox="0 0 48 90"><line x1="24" y1="0" x2="24" y2="30" stroke="#888878" stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.75"/><rect x="17" y="28" width="14" height="10" rx="2.5"fill="rgba(80,78,65,0.9)" stroke="rgba(160,155,120,0.7)" stroke-width="1"/><rect x="19" y="36" width="10" height="3" rx="1"fill="none" stroke="rgba(150,145,110,0.55)" stroke-width="0.8"/><ellipse cx="24" cy="60" rx="20" ry="22"fill="rgba(255,245,160,0.12)"/><path d="M24,38 C16,38 10,45 10,55 C10,67 16,78 24,78 C32,78 38,67 38,55 C38,45 32,38 24,38 Z"fill="rgba(255,252,210,0.95)" stroke="rgba(220,210,160,0.6)" stroke-width="0.8"/><ellipse cx="24" cy="57" rx="9" ry="11"fill="rgba(255,240,120,0.55)"/><path d="M18,60 L20,53 L24,58 L28,53 L30,60"fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,200,40,0.95)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/><rect x="20" y="75" width="8" height="3" rx="1"fill="rgba(200,195,155,0.65)" stroke="none"/></svg>
</div>
<div class="cellar-scene">
<div class="cellar-light"></div>

You bolt for the stairs. COPPER calls after you — half-genial, half-mocking — but you’re long gone, back through the door.

(if: $crossed is "john")[(set: $savedBy to "nobody")](else-if: $crossed is "ashton")[(set: $savedBy to "ashton")](else:)[(set: $savedBy to "john")]\
(if: $savedBy is "john")[
And through the door, leaning its knackered frame against his own, is JOHN ST. JOHN.

‘You lead a charmed life,’ he says.

(if: $metRed is true and $crossed is not "red")[JOHN falls in beside you as you push out onto Dean Street: ‘RED told COPPER you had money.’

You’re lucky, you reflect, that he worked out you don’t.](else-if: $crossed is "red")[He heard you rat on RED and it seems you impressed him.]

[[Back to Dean Street|The dark pass]]
](else-if: $savedBy is "ashton")[(set: $holdsAshtonName to true)
COPPER, fretful lion, shakes his jowls. ASHTON whispers something in his ear that seems to overfill him presto with a newly minted calm; such dreadful service must her lips have paid.

‘Maybe I rang customs,’ says ASHTON, the grinning tease. If she meant to confess then this is how she’d do it; but you can’t be sure what she means; you can’t even be sure that she knows what she means.

[[Out onto Dean Street|The dark pass]]
](else:)[
COPPER roars in the stairwell and shakes his jowls. His strength is in the singularity of revealed violence. Like all Godfathers he can stand alone; the firm’s a means to hurry things along or shift the blame. Just as the debt stands, so, at length, do you.

[[Out onto Dean Street|The dark pass]]
]
</div>

:: The dark pass [outdoor] {"position":"2300,1350","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-09: Red alone and the empty street were cut (his ruling), so when nobody got you out there is nothing to see here; straight back to Dean Street. -->
(unless: $savedBy is "john" or $savedBy is "ashton")[(go-to: "Dean Street")]\
<div class="typewriter-page dss-betrayal-aftermath">
(if: $savedBy is "john" and $crossed is not "red")[You watch JOHN ST. JOHN throw off his tail in the darkness, then surface again at the far end of the street, in the pool where the ginger light shines.

Just as he does, RED walks into the frame, hands deep in his pockets; fag in his mouth, swaying like a conductor’s baton.

It seems, almost, like RED wants to speak to JOHN, who doesn’t want to speak to anybody, and so ploughs his long stride deeper and into the night.
](else-if: $savedBy is "john")[JOHN throws off his tail and surfaces under the ginger light. Nobody walks into frame. JOHN notices that RED’S not on the streets tonight.
](else-if: $savedBy is "ashton")[As you step into the street you think that something scurries by you, like a cat escaping when its owner returns from the pub; you can’t be sure. Perhaps it was ASHTON GRANGER. If it was, she’ll now be past the ginger light, headed anywhere that’s very far away. You hope it was and that she will be safe.
]
[[Dean Street|Dean Street]]
</div>
<script>
// Light a cigarette of your own — Red is smoking, John has gone, you're
// alone on Dean Street and your hands need something to do. Auto-shows
// after the prose has had a beat to settle.
(function(){
  /* 2026-10-24 sweep: the snapshot ran before the MutationObserver had counted this passage, so the guard always tripped and the cigarette never came after the cellar (played live: nothing at 8 s). The outer setTimeout(0) defers the snapshot, as showDrinkPopupSafe and the Dawn do. */
  setTimeout(function(){
    var pgGen = window._passageGen;
    setTimeout(function(){
      if (window._passageGen !== pgGen) return;
      if (window.showCigarettePopup) window.showCigarettePopup();
    }, 5500);
  }, 0);
})();
</script>

