:: LINE 1 {"position":"700,200","size":"100,100"}
(set: $alba to $alba + (a: $alba1))
(set: $albaRevealed to true)
‘Forget the book,’ says RED, ‘it’s no way to live. Try this.’

As he turns from his ginger light he kisses you and, as he does, you close your eyes. Inside their shuttered lids you read:

<div class="revelation-box alba-fade-first" data-alba="1">
<em>‘$alba1’</em>
</div>

<strong class="alba-counter alba-fade-first">THE FIRST LINE OF THREE</strong>

<!-- 2026-10-28 (Sam, playtest notes 26/31: "What is Alba?", "explained FAR TOO LATE"): his three morning-song sentences moved here from Night Ahead Part Two, words unchanged --><div class="alba-why">The only way out is through a morning song.

