2" cy="44" r="0.7"/><circle cx="140" cy="32" r="0.5"/><circle cx="175" cy="48" r="0.6"/><circle cx="248" cy="26" r="0.8"/><circle cx="295" cy="41" r="0.5"/><circle cx="368" cy="30" r="0.7"/><circle cx="432" cy="45" r="0.5"/></g><rect width="500" height="110" fill="url(#gs2FH)"/><rect width="500" height="110" fill="url(#gs2FV)"/></svg>

Just off the beach is a bar called The Green Sea. It’s mostly old men playing cribbage, and on its wall is a portrait of Bourguiba.

At the back round the biggest table is a family you know, playing cards with an Italian deck.

Among them, with his back to you, is your old friend. The eldest of the children. You see him before he sees you.

<!-- HOUSE OF CARDS CUT, 2026-10-17 (Sam: "not that fun, just clutter"). The passage Green Sea House of Cards is kept whole below;
     to restore, put this link back here: [ [Build a house of cards|Green Sea House of Cards] ] (without the spaces inside the brackets). -->

<!-- SECOND LINE CUT HERE, 2026-10-09 (Sam, overnight brief: "just have it in the dream world"). The line used to be given
     here too, on "Listen"; it is now only at the centre of a dream world, so a complete poem needs the third pillar.
     His orphaned sentence ("He speaks. The family roars on round, as his sister winds a trick, but you hear this:") and the
     drunk-gate pink are kept in polish-loop/Structure pass orphans 2026-10-09.md. -->
[[Wake from this dream|LINE 2 Oxford]]

:: Green Sea House of Cards [green-sea]
<!-- HOUSE OF CARDS. Optional; never changes alba or sobriety.
     Sam approved 15 structural cards + 3 spares (2026-09-23).
     Dev only: DSS_DEV exposes _houseCardsDev angle/place/roar/snapshot;
     the testing skip returns without settling a reward. No retro music tag. -->
<div id="dss-house-cards">
<h2>HOUSE OF CARDS</h2>
<canvas width="600" height="430" tabindex="0" aria-label="House of cards: drag the foot to move the base, drag the body to tilt; Shift and arrow keys move the base, arrows tilt, Space sets the card."></canvas>
<div class="cards-meters"><span><small>Cards left</small><b class="cards-deck"></b></span><span><small>Standing</small><b class="cards-built"></b></span><span><small>Lean</small><b class="cards-angle"></b></span></div>
<div class="cards-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Stand a card on its edge.</div>
<div class="cards-controls"><button type="button" data-tilt="-2" aria-label="Tilt two degrees left">←</button><button type="button" class="cards-place">Place card</button><button type="button" data-tilt="2" aria-label="Tilt two degrees right">→</button></div>
<div class="cards-controls"><button type="button" data-base="-2">Base ←</button><button type="button" data-base="2">Base →</button></div>
<button type="button" class="cards-cancel" hidden>Take it back</button>
<div class="cards-payment" aria-hidden="true">
<span data-outcome="win">(link: "cards-win")[(unless: $houseCardsPlayed is true)[(set: $houseCardsPlayed to true)(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 8))<div class="inventory-note">MORALE +8</div>]<div>[[Back to the table|LINE 2]]</div>]</span>
<span data-outcome="excellent">(link: "cards-excellent")[(unless: $houseCardsPlayed is true)[(set: $houseCardsPlayed to true)(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 12))<div class="inventory-note">MORALE +12</div>]<div>[[Back to the table|LINE 2]]</div>]</span>
<span data-outcome="loss">(link: "cards-loss")[(unless: $houseCardsPlayed is true)[(set: $houseCardsPlayed to true)]<div>[[Back to the table|LINE 2]]</div>]</span>
</div>
<div class="cards-skip" hidden>[[(skip — testing)|LINE 2]]</div><span class="cards-again" hidden>[[Again|Green Sea House of Cards]]</span>
</div>
<!-- Timer starts at passage render, including time spent at the rules popup. -->
(after: 150s)[<div class="canvas-bail">[[Back to the table|LINE 2]]</div>]
<style>
#dss-house-cards{max-width:680px;width:100%;margin:24px auto;text-align:center;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Georgia,serif}
#dss-house-cards h2{font-size:clamp(22px,5vw,34px);letter-spacing:.13em;margin:12px 0}
#dss-house-cards > br,#dss-house-cards .cards-controls > br,#dss-house-cards .cards-meters > br{display:none}
#dss-house-cards canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:60/43;border:1px solid #887052;border-radius:8px;box-sizing:border-box;touch-action:none;background:#151713}
#dss-house-cards canvas:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #dfb978;outline-offset:3px}
#dss-house-cards .cards-meters{display:flex;gap:6px 16px;justify-content:space-between;padding:12px 2px 6px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
#dss-house-cards .cards-meters span{flex:1;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff16;padding-bottom:8px}
#dss-house-cards .cards-meters small{display:block;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.75}
#dss-house-cards .cards-meters b{display:block;font-weight:normal;font-size:clamp(20px,4vw,28px);margin-top:4px}
#dss-house-cards .cards-controls{display:flex;gap:10px;justify-content:center;margin:12px 0}
#dss-house-cards button{min-height:44px;min-width:48px;border:1px solid #87704d;border-radius:4px;background:#24231b;color:inherit;font:inherit;padding:8px 15px;touch-action:manipulation;cursor:pointer}
#dss-house-cards button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}
#dss-house-cards .cards-status{min-height:2.6em;font-size:clamp(16px,2.6vw,19px);line-height:1.45;padding-top:8px}
#dss-house-cards .cards-payment{display:none}
#dss-house-cards .cards-payment.revealed{display:block}
#dss-house-cards .cards-payment.revealed > span > tw-link,#dss-house-cards .cards-payment.revealed > span > tw-hook > tw-link{display:none}
#dss-house-cards [hidden]{display:none!important}
</style>
<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';
  var root = document.querySelector('tw-passage:last-of-type #dss-house-cards');
  if (!root || root.dataset.mounted) return;
  root.dataset.mounted = 'yes';
  var canvas = root.querySelector('canvas'), ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  if (!ctx) return; // Harlowe's independent 150-second escape still works.
  var W = 600, H = 430, L = 90, RAD = Math.PI / 180;
  // TUNING: score is initial angular accuracy, then cumulative tremor damage.
  var IDEAL = 70, LEAN_TOL = [15, 12, 9], MATCH_TOL = [12, 9, 6];
  var BRIDGE_TOL = [7, 5], INTERVAL = [8, 6.8, 5.6], DECK = 18;
  var DAMAGE = [.018, .023, .028], FINAL_DAMAGE = .12;
  /* 2026-10-28 (dssEase): an unfinished house makes the next one more forgiving: wider tolerances, slower and softer roars */
  var EZ = window.dssEase ? window.dssEase.level('cards') : 0;
  LEAN_TOL = LEAN_TOL.map(function(v){return v*(1+EZ*.2);}); MATCH_TOL = MATCH_TOL.map(function(v){return v*(1+EZ*.2);}); BRIDGE_TOL = BRIDGE_TOL.map(function(v){return v*(1+EZ*.2);});
  INTERVAL = INTERVAL.map(function(v){return v*(1+EZ*.12);}); DAMAGE = DAMAGE.map(function(v){return v*(1-EZ*.2);}); FINAL_DAMAGE *= (1-EZ*.2);
  var NUDGE_MIN = .2, NUDGE_RANGE = .6, PLACEMENT_QUIET = 1.5;
  var slots = [], placed = [], fallen = [], used = 0, falls = 0;
  var active = -1, angle = 60, elapsed = 0, nextRoar = 8, finalAt = 0;
  var editing = -1, pendingAngle = 60, houseReady = false;
  var baseX = 0, pendingBase = 0;
  var CONTACT_TOL = [18,15,12];
  var running = false, ended = false, disposed = false, frame = 0, last = 0;
  var flash = 0, warning = false, readyAt = 0, pointer = null, autoReturn = 0;
  var reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  var status = root.querySelector('.cards-status'), payment = root.querySelector('.cards-payment');
  var listeners = [], resizeObs, observer, dev;
  var endAt = 0, outcomeKind = '';
  // The game's own small sounds (dssAudio): a card set down, the table's thump, the glass.
  function sfx(name, delay) {
    var run = function () { if (disposed) return; try { var a = window.dssAudio; if (a && typeof a[name] === 'function') a[name](); } catch (e) {} };
    if (delay) setTimeout(run, delay); else run();
  }
  var cancel = root.querySelector('.cards-cancel');
  function listen(el, name, fn, options) { el.addEventListener(name, fn, options); listeners.push([el,name,fn,options]); }
  function say(text) { if (status.textContent !== text) status.textContent = text; }
  function clamp(v, a, b) { return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v)); }
  function addPair(level, center, supports) {
    var first = slots.length;
    slots.push({level:level, center:center, kind:'left', deps:supports.slice()});
    slots.push({level:level, center:center, kind:'right', deps:supports.concat(first), partner:first});
    return [first, first + 1];
  }
  var ground = [addPair(0,198,[]),addPair(0,300,[]),addPair(0,402,[])];
  function addBridge(level, left, right) {
    var id = slots.length;
    slots.push({level:level,kind:'bridge',left:left[0],right:right[0],deps:left.concat(right)});
    return id;
  }
  var b0 = addBridge(0,ground[0],ground[1]), b1 = addBridge(0,ground[1],ground[2]);
  var upper = [addPair(1,249,[b0]),addPair(1,351,[b1])];
  var b2 = addBridge(1,upper[0],upper[1]);
  addPair(2,300,[b2]);
  function liveCount() { return placed.filter(Boolean).length; }
  function currentLevel() { return active >= 0 ? slots[active].level : 2; }
  function eligible(i) { return !placed[i] && slots[i].deps.every(function(d){return !!placed[d];}); }
  function choose() {
    active = slots.findIndex(function(_,i){return eligible(i);});
    houseReady = active < 0;
    if (houseReady) { say('The house is built. Face the roar when ready.'); return; }
    angle = slots[active].kind === 'bridge' ? (used % 2 ? -8 : 8) : (used % 2 ? 80 : 60);
    baseX = suggestedBase(active);
    say(slots[active].kind === 'bridge' ? 'Lay a card across the pair.' : slots[active].kind === 'right' ? 'Lean this card towards its partner.' : 'Stand a card on its edge.');
  }
  function cardAngle(i) { return i === editing ? angle : placed[i].angle; }
  function angleQuality(i, value) {
    var s = slots[i], ideal = s.kind === 'bridge' ? 0 : IDEAL;
    var tol = s.kind === 'bridge' ? BRIDGE_TOL[s.level] : LEAN_TOL[s.level];
    var error = Math.abs(value-ideal)/tol;
    var mate = s.kind === 'right' ? s.partner : s.kind === 'left' ? i+1 : -1;
    if (mate >= 0 && placed[mate]) error = Math.max(error,Math.abs(value-placed[mate].angle)/MATCH_TOL[s.level]);
    var g=geometry(i,value);
    if(mate>=0 && placed[mate]) {
      var m=geometry(mate,cardAngle(mate));
      error=Math.max(error,Math.hypot(g.tx-m.tx,g.ty-m.ty)/CONTACT_TOL[s.level]);
    }
    if(s.kind==='bridge') {
      var left=geometry(s.left,cardAngle(s.left)),right=geometry(s.right,cardAngle(s.right));
      error=Math.max(error,Math.abs(g.x-left.tx)/18,Math.hypot(g.tx-right.tx,g.ty-(right.ty-3))/18);
    }
    return {valid:error < 1 && (s.kind === 'bridge' || (value > 55 && value < 85)),stability:Math.max(0,1-.85*error)};
  }
  function selectCard(i) {
    if (!running || ended || finalAt || !placed[i]) return;
    if (editing < 0) { pendingAngle = angle; pendingBase = baseX; }
    editing = i; angle = placed[i].angle; baseX = placed[i].base;
    say('');
    update(); draw();
  }
  function cancelEdit() {
    if (editing < 0) return;
    editing = -1; angle = pendingAngle; baseX = pendingBase;
    nextRoar = Math.max(nextRoar,elapsed+PLACEMENT_QUIET);
    say(houseReady?'The house is built. Face the roar when ready.':'');
    update(); draw();
  }
  // Stored feet are independent of lean angle. Upper feet are measured along
  // their supporting bridge, so moving a support carries its upper cards.
  function support(i) {
    var s=slots[i];
    if(s.kind==='bridge') {
      var l=geometry(s.left,cardAngle(s.left)),r=geometry(s.right,cardAngle(s.right));
      return {x:l.tx,y:l.ty-3,slope:0,width:Math.max(12,r.tx-l.tx),length:Math.hypot(r.tx-l.tx,r.ty-l.ty)};
    }
    if(s.level) {
      var floor=geometry(s.deps[0],cardAngle(s.deps[0]));
      return {x:floor.x,y:floor.y-3,slope:(floor.ty-floor.y)/(floor.tx-floor.x),width:floor.tx-floor.x};
    }
    return {x:0,y:363,slope:0,width:W};
  }
  function baseLimits(i) {
    var s=slots[i],f=support(i);
    return s.kind==='bridge'?[-17,17]:s.level?[3,Math.max(3,f.width-3)]:[40,W-40];
  }
  function suggestedBase(i) {
    var s=slots[i],f=support(i),half=L*Math.cos(IDEAL*RAD),x;
    if(s.kind==='bridge')x=0;
    else if(s.kind==='right') {
      var partner=geometry(s.partner,cardAngle(s.partner));
      x=partner.tx+(partner.tx-partner.x)-f.x;
    } else x=(s.level?f.width/2:s.center)-half;
    var limits=baseLimits(i);return clamp(x,limits[0],limits[1]);
  }
  function geometry(i, a) {
    var s=slots[i],f=support(i);
    var base=i===editing || (!placed[i] && i===active)?baseX:placed[i].base;
    var x=f.x+base,y=f.y+base*f.slope;
    var theta=(s.kind==='bridge'?-a:s.kind==='left'?-a:a-180)*RAD;
    var length=s.kind==='bridge'?f.length:L;
    return {x:x,y:y,tx:x+Math.cos(theta)*length,ty:y+Math.sin(theta)*length,theta:theta,length:length};
  }
  function tumble(ids) {
    var broken = new Set(ids);
    slots.forEach(function(s,i){if(placed[i] && s.deps.some(function(d){return broken.has(d);})) broken.add(i);});
    // Snapshot before removing supports, so every falling card has valid geometry.
    broken.forEach(function(i){if(placed[i]) fallen.push({g:geometry(i,placed[i].angle),suit:i%4,t:elapsed});});
    var n=0;broken.forEach(function(i){if(placed[i]){placed[i]=null;falls++;if(n<5)sfx('cardTurn',n*70);n++;}});
  }
  function place() {
    if (!running || ended || finalAt || document.hidden || elapsed < readyAt) return;
    if (editing >= 0) {
      var quality = angleQuality(editing,angle);
      if (!quality.valid) { say('The cards don’t meet.'); return; }
      var i = editing, previous = placed[i].angle, previousBase = placed[i].base;
      placed[i].angle = angle; placed[i].base = baseX;
      // A real adjustment re-seats the card. Merely tapping it does not heal it.
      if (Math.abs(previous-angle) > .1 || Math.abs(previousBase-baseX) > .1) placed[i].stability = quality.stability;
      sfx('cardTurn');
      cancelEdit(); readyAt = elapsed + .3; return;
    }
    if (houseReady) { finalAt = elapsed + 1.2; say('His sister winds a trick…'); update(); return; }
    if (active < 0) return;
    var i = active, quality = angleQuality(i,angle), valid = quality.valid;
    used++; sfx('cardTurn');
    if (valid) placed[i] = {angle:angle,base:baseX,stability:quality.stability};
    else { fallen.push({g:geometry(i,angle),suit:i%4,t:elapsed}); falls++; }
    readyAt = elapsed + .3;
    nextRoar = Math.max(nextRoar,elapsed+PLACEMENT_QUIET);
    choose();
    if (!valid) say('It slips.');
    if (used >= DECK && liveCount() < slots.length) finish('loss');
    update(); draw();
  }
  function roar(final) {
    if (editing >= 0 || pointer) return;
    flash = .6; sfx('muffledThud'); if (final) sfx('glassClink',160);
    var level = currentLevel(), broken = [];
    placed.forEach(function(card,i){
      if (!card) return;
      var nudge = (NUDGE_MIN+Math.random()*NUDGE_RANGE) * (1+level*.08);
      card.angle += (Math.random()<.5 ? -1 : 1) * nudge;
      card.stability -= (final ? FINAL_DAMAGE : DAMAGE[level]) * (.85+nudge/8);
      if (card.stability <= 0) broken.push(i);
    });
    tumble(broken);
    if (final) { finish(liveCount()===slots.length ? (falls===0?'excellent':'win') : 'loss'); return; }
    if (broken.length) { choose(); say('The table roars. Part of the house comes down.'); }
    else say('The roar passes.');
    nextRoar = elapsed + INTERVAL[currentLevel()] + Math.random() * .8;
    if (used >= DECK && liveCount() < slots.length) finish('loss');
    update();
  }
  function finish(outcome) {
    if (ended || disposed) return;
    ended = true; running = false; pointer = null; endAt = elapsed; outcomeKind = outcome;
    if (outcome !== 'loss') sfx('brightChord',380);
    say(outcome === 'excellent' ? 'Not one card fell.' : outcome === 'win' ? 'The house stands.' : 'The house is unfinished.');
    root.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(function(b){b.disabled=true;});
    /* 2026-10-28 (Sam: "Easier each retry"): an unfinished house offers TRY AGAIN (a gentler house, the page entered afresh) or MOVE ON (as before) */
    if (outcome === 'loss' && window.dssEase && !window.dssEase._cardsMove) {
      window.dssEase.lost('cards');
      var cvC = root.querySelector('canvas');
      setTimeout(function(){
        if (!root.isConnected) return;
        window.dssEase.offer(cvC.parentElement, { onAgain: function(){ var a = root.parentElement.querySelector('.cards-again tw-link') || document.querySelector('.cards-again tw-link'); if (a) a.click(); }, onMove: function(){ ended = false; window.dssEase._cardsMove = true; finish('loss'); window.dssEase._cardsMove = false; } });
      }, 900);
      draw();
      return;
    }
    var target = payment.querySelector('[data-outcome="'+outcome+'"] tw-link');
    if (target) target.click();
    payment.classList.add('revealed'); payment.removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
    // Let the inventory note be seen; the real Harlowe return link stays usable if this fails.
    autoReturn = setTimeout(function(){
      if (!root.isConnected) return;
      var back = payment.querySelector('[data-outcome="'+outcome+'"] tw-hook tw-link');
      if (back) back.click();
