<!-- 2026-10-16 (Sam: restore): the hearing of the dawn, from the 15 April backup, words unchanged -->If dawn was something you could hear, you would hear it now. Your ears are attuned in a way that your eyes can never be. But you trust your eyes more, so the thrum of dawn approaching, registers as a silent alarm.

You see it, the sky tearing patches from itself and bleeding red, orange, green through night’s bandage.

(link: "Closer")[(set: $alba to $alba + (a: $alba3))
The last line comes out of your own throat, as you cry, ‘I wish that I was never…’ then:

<div class="revelation-box" data-alba="3">
<em>‘$alba3’</em>
</div>

(if: ($alba contains $alba1) and ($alba contains $alba2))[It is written. You shall get out alive.

<strong class="alba-counter">THE THIRD LINE. THE ALBA IS COMPLETE.</strong>

](else:)[<strong class="alba-counter">THE THIRD LINE.</strong>

There are still lines hidden in the night.

]

