:: O'Flatterly introduction [venue-cecilcourt char-inis threshold] {"position":"300,1700","size":"100,100"}
<span class="shop-bell-marker" style="display:none">(if: $returnedPage is true)[post](else-if: $hasMissingPage is true)[has-page](else:)[pre]</span>(display: "Cecil Rule SVG")
INIS O’FLATTERLY clocks you, first with his eyes still downcast, then eventually as he looks up. ‘You’re a novelist and that wasn’t a question,’ he steams; with the gentle steaming of the kettle, not that of the railway.

(if: $hasMissingPage is true)[You hand him the page.

[[Show him the page|Return the page]]]\
(else:)[[[Speak to him|O'Flatterly's quest]]]

:: O'Flatterly's quest [venue-cecilcourt char-inis threshold] {"position":"300,1850","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-25 (Sam, ordering audit 2B): the refusal and its slip only while the book is in the bag; the rest of the scene stands -->(set: _bagBook to ((($bookAt is not a string) or ($bookAt is "")) and ($bookSold is not true) and (($bookLent is not a string) or ($bookLent is ""))))‘Dear boy,’ he burrs, ‘I don’t know who you are, and don’t care who you are(if: _bagBook)[, and I don’t know that I don’t like what you’ve written; but do me a kindness, kid, and let’s just assume I won’t need it]. Besides, there is something that you must do for me, that we must do together.’(if: _bagBook)[<span class="dss-refusal" data-k="inis" data-who="INIS O’FLATTERLY" hidden>‘I don’t know that I don’t like what you’ve written; but do me a kindness, kid, and let’s just assume I won’t need it.’</span>]

O’Flatterly coughs, disturbing the dust on the cover before him, agitating its thousand motes into flight, which hang over his desk like the clouds over Willesden Junction.

He slaps the manuscript like an arse and says: <span class="dss-speech" data-speaker="INIS O’FLATTERLY" style="--sp:#8fbf78"><span class="dss-quest-line">‘Page 93 is missing. Find it for me!’</span></span><!-- 2026-10-23 overnight: the errand itself, in the quest-line gold, now that its card waits for "I’ll look for it" --><span class="dss-refusal-after" data-k="inis" hidden>You can swallow that; he’s neither publisher nor agent, and besides he’ll give you more than he could if he were. You’ll take the book and chance your arm elsewhere.</span>

(set: $knowsAboutPage to true)

