:: O'Flatterly's Third Pillar [venue-cecilcourt char-inis] {"position":"600,1950","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-28: the second half of O'Flatterly's Gift (Sam's words unchanged), split so each page fits a laptop screen -->(set: $inisToldOfPillars to true)\
<div>
INIS looks at the door and then at you.
<!-- 2026-10-29 (Sam, playtest note 14, the mock-up approved): plot speech from someone in the game world sits in a speaker's panel; his words unchanged --><div class="dss-speech" data-speaker="INIS O’FLATTERLY" style="--sp:#8fbf78">‘There’s something they don’t say about the Pillars of Hercules,’ he begins, his thumbnails sitting on the counter’s lip. ‘The legends speak of two pillars only: one at Gibraltar, the other on the shores of the Maghreb. These are on either side of the pub’s front door.

‘But there were always three. Most people go a lifetime without ever seeing the third. I’ve been here so long, longer than a lifetime perhaps, that I have seen the third that stands between them.

‘Step into the third and you will find new worlds, such as were never dreamed between the Tyburn and the Fleet.

‘And know this too: the third blue post is hungry; be sure to have some offering to charm your way to the far side of the veil. You’ll find what you need as you wander; pay attention.

‘In fact there could be something in my shop that pays your way, though I wouldn’t look here first; you must explore. And if you find it standing, dear boy, go through.’</div>
</div>

