<!-- 2026-10-16 (Sam: restore, "some of the best writing I had done"): from the 15 April backup, words unchanged; the cow now lives in the Coach, so the way back is to the bar -->(set: $milkedCow to true)\
(set: $sobriety to ($statGain: $sobriety, 15))\
(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 10))\
<h2 class="venue-title">The Coach and Horses</h2>
You lie on the Dean Street pavement like a mechanic under a chassis, take an udder in your fist and squeeze it, gingerly.

A little warm milk plashes on your lips. It tastes of grass and moonlight and something you can’t name.

‘This,’ you think, ‘is why he is unwell.’

<!-- 2026-10-23 overnight (Sam, playtest: "'Milk her' should throw you out of the pub, not back to the bar. Then you can reenter"): you are on the pavement, so the link leaves you outside the Coach -->[[Get up and try again|Approach The Coach]]

