<!-- NEW-GAME RESETS 2026-09-13. All of these were declared only by
     type-guards of the "set it if it is not already an array" kind, which fire
     the first time a variable is created and so never fire on a replay in the
     same browser: a second playthrough inherited the first one's state. Found
     when a new game opened with Meard Street and Walker's Court already walked.
     The alleys were the least of it. Keys left as spent meant a replay could
     begin with no pocket-keys at all, which shuts the third pillar for a whole
     night; a stolen notebook meant starting without one; and a full
     worldsVisited shuts the pillar on its own five-world guard.
     NB: do not write macro syntax inside these comments. Harlowe parses macros
     inside HTML comments, and an example macro written here swallowed every set
     below it, silently and with no error. That is how this very block failed
     the first time. -->\
