(else-if: _fc <= 1 and ($frenchProseShown is not true))[(set: $frenchProseShown to true)As you walk in the bar drops down to silence, as if its speech were interrupted by a quick gasp for breath, the way a doe sometimes mistakes the wind in the grass for a wolf, stiffens, then goes about its day.<!-- 2026-10-16 (Sam: "the first thing you saw when you entered the French ... some of my best writing"): the bar as it stood on the first visit in April, restored here from the 2026-04-15 backup; the painter's card keeps its own copy -->

At one end of the bar are the artists; you know them, they are famous.

Stuffed into a barstool which his arsecheeks overhang, like clouds waiting to rain, is a stout man with his back to you. His leather jacket, somehow both parched and sweating, falls short at the neck, flashing a collar of labial pink.

Opposite him is the only man who looks you in the eyes, who is thin like verdaccio and hardly there at all.]
