(set: $visitedInterval to true)\
(set: $visitedCarthage to true)\
Salt on the lip. Cinder in the lashes. The pyre’s heat lifts from your face the way a hand lifts from your face — and you wake.

A flight of stairs, the kind you find leaving a theatre; red carpet worn thin as your world in its dead middle. Brass banister under your hand, still warm from other hands. Somewhere, a radio is playing spare: Love, O careless Love…

[[Continue|The Interval: the stairs]]


:: The Interval: the stairs [interval-radio] {"position":"900,300","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-29 (Sam, playtest note 11: "too much prose on this page. It should be broken up"): the Interval in two; LILY on the stairs is its second page, words unchanged -->(if: $intervalStairsSeen is true)[(go-to: "Dean Street")](set: $intervalStairsSeen to true)\
<div class="lily-window">
A woman passes; she is going up. Two steps down you freeze, stopped clock, right twice: you’d know that perfume anywhere. It’s LILY.
<!-- 2026-10-16 (Sam: restore): the glimpse of the third line and the Yeats, from the 15 April backup's Interval, words unchanged -->You catch a third line: <span class="lily-thought">‘She lay beside me in the dawn.’</span> The words aren’t yours to keep yet.
<span class="lily-thought">And with it, her risen face:</span>
<div class="verse">That is not natural in an age like this,<br>Being high and solitary and most stern</div>
(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 12))\
(set: $sobriety to ($statGain: $sobriety, 10))\
She goes upstairs. You go down.
<span class="lily-thought">(link: "Turn and follow her")[<span class="lily-fade-in">You take the stairs by doubles but when you get there she’s gone. Lily-of-the-Valley is all that remains on the spendthrift draught.</span>(if: $sawMemory3 is false)[(set: $sawMemory3 to true)<div class="memory-photo memory-photo-3"><div class="mp-image"><svg class="mp-bg" viewBox="0 0 300 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"><defs><radialGradient id="fl3" cx="50%" cy="40%" r="88%"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#f8c8a8" stop-opacity="1"/><stop offset="22%" stop-color="#e89878" stop-opacity="0.78"/><stop offset="52%" stop-color="#a05060" stop-opacity="0.32"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#1a0a18" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient></defs><rect width="300" height="200" fill="url(#fl3)"/></svg><div class="mp-prose">In a certain memory she sits on your bed, dressing; she is in her underwear, which is filigree and black. Since then, and before it, life has rarely been so real. You’d burn Troy after Troy to see God’s face again.</div></div></div>]

<span class="alba-link-fade">[[Down again.|Dean Street]]</span>]</span>
</div>

