<!-- Lattice pub window at top -->
<svg class="pillars-lattice" viewBox="0 0 300 36" width="100%" height="36" preserveAspectRatio="none"><defs><linearGradient id="latEdgeb" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0%"   stop-color="#7ab8cc" stop-opacity="0"/><stop offset="15%"  stop-color="#7ab8cc" stop-opacity="0.55"/><stop offset="85%"  stop-color="#7ab8cc" stop-opacity="0.55"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#7ab8cc" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient><pattern id="dLat" x="0" y="0" width="42" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M7,0 L14,12 L7,24 L0,12 Z" fill="rgba(160,35,25,0.26)" stroke="#5a96aa" stroke-width="1" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M21,0 L28,12 L21,24 L14,12 Z" fill="rgba(185,215,235,0.07)" stroke="#5a96aa" stroke-width="1" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M35,0 L42,12 L35,24 L28,12 Z" fill="rgba(28,108,52,0.22)" stroke="#5a96aa" stroke-width="1" stroke-linejoin="round"/></pattern><mask id="latMask"><rect x="0" y="0" width="300" height="36" fill="url(#latEdgeb)"/></mask></defs><g filter="url(#dss-ink-fine)"><rect x="0" y="0" width="300" height="36" fill="url(#dLat)" mask="url(#latMask)"/><line x1="0" y1="34" x2="300" y2="34" stroke="url(#latEdgeb)" stroke-width="1.2"/></g></svg>
<div class="ham-callback-stage" hidden aria-hidden="true"></div><!-- a "-stage" marker keeps this page out of the plain-page panel, as its first half is (the book stage), so the scene looks the same across the split and THE RUMOUR card opens as before --><div class="critic-aftermath revealed" id="critAftermath"><div class="critic-after-verdict"><!-- 2026-10-17 (Sam's line, the worlds wired to the readers): --><span class="dss-gift-line" data-gift="himalayas" hidden>‘Looks like you found thunder on the mountain. It still won’t sell but, if it’s any consolation, it’ll keep.’<br><br></span>(if: $mantraComplete is true)[<span class="dss-gift-now" data-gift="himalayas" hidden></span>]<span class="dss-speech" data-speaker="THE GREAT HAM" style="--sp:#d9806a"><span class="dss-quest-line">‘When you’re next in Cecil Court, look for INIS O’FLATTERLY. Quare fellow, knows a lot about books. I think he’d like to meet you. He’s been trying to get to Carthage, on his way to The Pillars of Hercules.’</span></span>
<!-- 2026-10-11, Sam: the venue-opens line wherever a new venue opens. The header back-fills $knowsCecilCourt as soon as $metCritic is true, so this keys on its own once-flag; the novelist carries his own line inside the haunt box. -->\
(if: $cecilOpensSaid is not true)[(if: not ($haunts contains $haunt2))[(set: $cecilOpensSaid to true)<div class="haunt-opens">Cecil Court opens.</div>]]
(set: $knowsCecilCourt to true)\
<!-- 2026-10-09, Sam: the ship rumour comes in the call-back, before midnight only; two versions by whether you have been down to the cellar yet. -->\
(if: $shipNews is "" and $afterMidnight is false)[(set: $shipNews to "rumour")(set: $hamRumour to true)(if: $metSalvu is false)[<!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam, A and B): his speech, words unchanged, broken into paragraphs and set on a card, THE RUMOUR, that opens over the page a moment after; the small link reopens it (dssRumourCard) -->He leans low on his elbows and whispers, stagily, <span class="rumour-open" role="button" tabindex="0">THE RUMOUR</span><div class="rumour-text" hidden><p>‘Let me tell you something I’ve heard tonight.</p><p>‘I believe you are familiar with ASHTON GRANGER. God love her: SALVU COPPER, the Maltese gangster, heard she has a few quid to spare. She’s been courting one of his muscle men, QUIET FRANKIE.</p><p>‘Long story short, they charmed her into buying a shipment of “pipe cleaners” – Lord knows what it really is – that’s been on its way to Liverpool from America. Thing is, it’s meant to dock tonight and SALVU’S got the shivers, he hasn’t heard word of progress and thinks they’re all frightened to tell him it’s sunk.</p><p>‘So SALVU’S got QUIET FRANKIE holding ASHTON GRANGER hostage, though she doesn’t know she’s a hostage, in his cellar under Dean Street. If the ship comes in she’ll never know a thing.</p><p>‘Now, you didn’t hear a word of that; I assume that we’d both like to see the morning.’</p></div><script>setTimeout(function(){ if (window.dssRumourCard) window.dssRumourCard(); }, 0);</script>](else:)[‘Do you know anyone who can clean a dirty pipe?’]]<!-- 2026-10-21 (Sam, playtest: "the order is wrong here ... he knows it on the first meeting"): his aside about COPPER, and the password it carries, now come after the rumour that first names COPPER; the sentence is his, unchanged, with its own quote marks; same gate as before (not once SALVU has been met) -->(if: $metSalvu is false)[

‘And if you see COPPER, tell him I said hello.’

(if: $knowsCopperWord is false)[<div class="item-box critic-deferred-motes">
<div class="item-header">PASSWORD LEARNED</div>
<div class="item-name">“I said hello”</div>
<div class="item-note">It&#39;s saved in your notebook <span class="item-note-arrow">&#8593;</span></div>
</div>
(set: $knowsCopperWord to true)]]<!-- 2026-10-23 (Sam, playtest: "the slip ... repeats the 'america' type words, they shouldn't be happening twice in one scene"): the slip asks "Have you tried America?" and the reply above answers it ("America, you think of new-found-land."), so this after-line, a third America, is kept here but not shown --><span class="dss-ham-america-echo" hidden>Perhaps you’ll try America after all.</span>\
<!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam: "you have to really want to sell the book"): straight after the Ham's refusal, home rings: AOIFE's call, the same card as the Pillars', brought in once the verdict, its slip and any rumour card have passed (the hidden link is pressed by the script below) -->(if: ($hadPhoneCall is false) and ($ringSnoozed is not true))[<span class="ham-ring-go" hidden>(link: "ham-ring-go")[(replace: ?hamring)[<div class="phone-ringing ring-now">Behind the bar a phone rings and your name is called.

<!-- 2026-10-24 (Sam, playtest: "You have the option to 'leave the pub' from the Ham. Then you see the rumour then the phonecall. It shouldn't take you back to the bar after that, it should eject you"): when the ring came because you made to leave, #critAftermath carries .ham-leaving, which shows the -leave-only links: the call hangs up onto the street, a refusal has no way back to the bar -->|hamaoifering>[<span class="ham-stay-only">(link: "Accept the call")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 9))(go-to: "The phone call")]</span><span class="ham-leave-only">(link: "Accept the call")[(set: $callThenOut to true)(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 9))(go-to: "The phone call")]</span>
(link: "I’m not here")[(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 4))(display: "Bars Now")(unless: $refusedCalls is a num)[(set: $refusedCalls to 0)](set: $refusedCalls to $refusedCalls + 1)(set: $ringSnoozed to true)(set: $resumingFromCall to true)(set: $refusedAoife to true)(replace: ?hamaoifering)[The barman looks you over utterly neutrally. He wishes he wasn’t paid to be part of this game. ‘Not seen him,’ he says, and puts back the receiver.
(if: $refusedCalls is 2)[<div class="glass-pane">(display: "Fetch Window SVG")</div>]
<span class="ham-stay-only">[[Back to the bar|Entering The Pillars of Hercules]]</span>]]]</div>]]</span>]|hamring>[]\
[[Leave the pub.|Dean Street]]
</div></div>
</div>

<script>
(function(){
  // 2026-10-14: AOIFE rings once the verdict is filed and the rumour card (if any) has been read and closed
  // 2026-10-23 (Sam: "fix the missable Aoife call first"): a way out could beat the ring (the street exit is live while the
  // slip flies, "Leave the pub." before the rumour is closed), and a missed ring came back only on a later Pillars entry, so
  // LILY never rang either. While the ring is still due, making to leave brings it in instead (at once if the page is clear,
  // else as soon as it is); once it has rung, the ways out leave as before. On window, so it hears the click before the
  // departure fade's document listener, which would otherwise hold the press and replay it after the ring.
  var t0 = Date.now(), seenRumour = false, leaving = false;
  function clear(af) { return !!(af && af.classList.contains('revealed') && !document.querySelector('.dss-slip-fly, #dss-lore-overlay')); }
  function onExit(e) {
    var go = document.querySelector('.ham-ring-go tw-link');
    if (!go || !go.isConnected) { window.removeEventListener('click', onExit, true); return; }
    var l = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('tw-link');
    if (!l || !/Out onto the street|Leave the pub/.test(l.textContent)) return;
    e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); leaving = true;
    var af = document.getElementById('critAftermath'); if (af) af.classList.add('ham-leaving');
    /* 2026-10-24 (Sam, playtest: "the romour does show as you leave. This is correct ... the telephone shouldn't ring till you close the rumour"): an unread rumour opens now, and the ring waits behind it */
    var rt = document.querySelector('.rumour-text');
    if (rt && !rt._read && window._dssRumourNow) { window._dssRumourNow(); return; }
    if (clear(af)) { clearInterval(iv); go.click(); }
  }
  window.addEventListener('click', onExit, true);
  var iv = setInterval(function() {
    var go = document.querySelector('.ham-ring-go tw-link'), af = document.getElementById('critAftermath');
    if (!go || !go.isConnected) { if (Date.now() - t0 > 4000) clearInterval(iv); return; }
    if (!af || !af.classList.contains('revealed')) return;
    if (document.querySelector('.dss-slip-fly, #dss-lore-overlay')) { seenRumour = seenRumour || !!document.getElementById('dss-lore-overlay'); return; }
    var rt = document.querySelector('.rumour-text'); if (rt && !rt._read) return; /* 2026-10-24: the ring waits until the rumour has been read and closed, leaving or not */
    clearInterval(iv); setTimeout(function() { if (go.isConnected) go.click(); }, leaving ? 200 : 1400);
  }, 300);
})();
</script>

:: The novelist [venue-french char-novelist] {"position":"700,550","size":"100,100"}
(display: "French Rule SVG h60")
(set: $confidence to ($statLoss: $confidence, 9))
He’s been reading it for longer than is comfortable for either of you.

At last, he pushes it back and asks: ‘Is this yours?’

Before you can answer, he says, ‘I don’t know.’<span class="dss-refusal" data-k="novelist" data-who="THE NOVELIST" hidden>‘Is this yours?’ ‘I don’t know.’</span><span class="dss-refusal-after" data-k="novelist" hidden>Fair’s fair; you’ve only got back what you gave. No matter, you’ll keep on.</span>

(if: not ($haunts contains $haunt2))[
(set: $haunts to $haunts + (a: $haunt2))
<!-- THE REFUSAL is what opens Cecil Court (2026-09-13). The box below has always
     said so; the hub was gating on $knowsCecilCourt, which only the critic set,
     so the promise went unkept and the court stayed shut until mid-game. -->
(set: $knowsCecilCourt to true)\
<div class="haunt-box">
<div class="haunt-header">⟡ HAUNT COLLECTED ⟡</div>
<div class="haunt-name">THE REFUSAL</div>
<div class="haunt-description">Have a glass of water.</div>
<div class="haunt-work"><em>The work: Solutio.</em></div>
<div class="haunt-opens">You know Cecil Court very well.</div>
<div class="haunt-progress">(print: $haunts's length) of 12 caught</div>(display: "Mantra Syllable Cue")
</div>
(if: $haunts's length is 1)[(set: $hauntExplained to true)(if: $hauntPrimerShown is not true)[(set: $hauntPrimerShown to true)<script>setTimeout(function(){ if(window.dssShowHauntPrimer) window.dssShowHauntPrimer(); }, 3500);</script>](if: $primerShown is false)[(set: $primerShown to true)<script>setTimeout(function(){ if(window.dssShowPrimer) window.dssShowPrimer(); }, 1600);</script>]]]

