:: Airport Pub [dream himalayan] {"position":"700,2200","size":"100,100"}
<div id="ap-container"></div>
<div class="airport-pub-scene">
<div class="ap-prose">
The Enlightenment has been in the Departure Lounge for as long as anyone can remember. Some claim they’ve found it shut but nobody believes them. It hums in the ear and the nose, settled as a fixture. There is jet fuel in the lager that gets you drunk.

The best drink is the drink-in-transit and this is the Wembley Stadium of such boozing. No point talking to strangers; anyone you meet will be half the world away come sun-up, somewhere. No, here we keep time to ourselves and watch for ‘Go to Gate’.

A man sits in a booth reading //Chariots of the Gods?//
(link: "⟡ LORE: Chariots of the Gods? ⟡")[(set: _lore to "Chariots of the Gods?")(display: "Lore Read")<div class="lore-box">(display: "Lore Chariots of the Gods")</div>]

He doesn’t introduce himself. His eyes are slate, and kind.

‘Half,’ he says, and writes on a napkin: Datta. Dayadhvam. Damyata. ‘The rest is in the mountains, with me where the road ends.’
</div>

(if: $mantraHalf1 is false)[(set: $mantraHalf1 to true)
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">HALF A MANTRA</div>
<div class="item-name">Datta. Dayadhvam. Damyata.</div>
</div>
]

<div>[[Final call|The Road to India]]</div>
</div>

:: The Road to India [dream himalayan] {"position":"900,2200","size":"100,100"}
<div>
The road gives up three times in feint before it gives up for good. On the dashboard there is a photo of Dodi Fayed and Princess Diana. You are deep now, deep in the wild.

At Manali the bus stops one last time and since the road goes up, you walk.
</div>

<div>[[Into the foothills|Foothills]]</div>

:: Foothills [dream himalayan] {"position":"1100,2200","size":"100,100"}
<div>
The thinning air in the foothills is wholly provisional; it wants you to leave.

You climb through villages and animals. A woman gives you tea with salt and butter. At last the pines give out and there is nobody else. Only you and the weather, which at this altitude gives you fair warning of its approach.

Prayer flags crosshatch the path with unlikely anchors. Sometimes you think you can see the curve of the earth in the dumb horizon’s giving blue.

You come to a fork. One path keeps climbing, the other curls back on the safe and imaginable valleys, and beyond them, home.
</div>

<div>[[Keep climbing|The Mountain]]
[[Turn back|Himalayan Turn-Back]]</div>

:: The Mountain [dream himalayan] {"position":"1300,2200","size":"100,100"}
<!-- The cost-of-passage moment. Climbing the mountain takes something from
     you. No fail state — the player commits and pays. Dr Quill can later
     add a real test (stat check, minigame, choice) in place of the
     simple stat costs below. -->
(set: $sobriety to $sobriety - 12)\
(set: $confidence to $confidence - 9)\
<div>
You crest another ridge (which must be but isn’t the last) and something is moving on the clean snow above you at a steady pace and not looking round.
</div>
<span class="inventory-note">SOBRIETY -12 | MORALE -9</span>

<div>[[Follow him|The Climb]]</div>

:: The Cave [dream himalayan cave] {"position":"1500,2200","size":"100,100"}
<!-- The completion passage. Click "Say the mantra" reveals the mandala
     portal and routes back to Soho via Himalayan Return. Sets the
     completion flags + adds himalayas to $worldsVisited + clears
     $tonightsWorld so a new world can roll on next Pillars visit. -->
<div>
The cave is lucid and warm and feels somehow lived-in, not only by its present occupant but by a thousand generations of upright apes, most unknown and unknowable to Western science.

A butter lamp burns in a niche and near it, sitting in the lotus with the paperback, //Chariots of the Gods?// open on his knees, which were recently departed by a small black cat, is the slate-eyed man who you met a long while ago in The Enlightenment.
(link: "⟡ LORE: Chariots of the Gods? ⟡")[(set: _lore to "Chariots of the Gods?")(display: "Lore Read")<div class="lore-box">(display: "Lore Chariots of the Gods")</div>]

‘Sorry about all the mess,’ he says. ‘Say it!’
</div>

(link: "Say the mantra")[
(set: $mantraHalf2 to true)\
(if: $himalayaClimbWon is true)[(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 8))(display: "Bars Now")<div class="inventory-note">MORALE +8</div>]\
(set: $mantraComplete to true)\
(unless: $worldsVisited contains "himalayas")[(set: $worldsVisited to $worldsVisited + (a: "himalayas"))]
(set: $tonightsWorld to "")\
<script>if(window.dssMarkWorldSeen)window.dssMarkWorldSeen("himalayas");</script>\
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">MANTRA COMPLETED</div>
<div class="item-name">Datta. Dayadhvam. Damyata. Shantih shantih shantih</div>
</div>

<!-- v2-expansion: the binding-revelation moment. Player sees that the
     syllables they've been "hearing" with each haunt are this mantra. -->
<div>
You say it, thunderously. You have said it before, a thousand times, but never considered its meaning.
</div>

(if: $haunts is an array and $haunts's length > 0)[<div class="nb-mantra-row" style="margin: 1em auto 1.5em;">(for: each _i, ...(range: 1, $mantra's length))[(if: _i <= $haunts's length)[<span class="nb-mantra-syl heard">(print: _i of $mantra)</span>](else:)[<span class="nb-mantra-syl silent">·</span>]]</div>]

