<script>
if (window.dssAudio && window.dssAudio.loreUnravel) {
  setTimeout(function(){ window.dssAudio.loreUnravel(); }, 200);
}
</script>

<div>
A bright mandala draws itself extrinsically. Your own hand is in it already and always was.
</div>

<!-- ALBA 2 ATTEND-MOMENT (phase 2, 2026-09-01): the second line is latent in every world centre,
     earned by a quiet attend-choice in the world's register (the Green Sea "Listen" pattern). Pink draft. -->
(unless: $alba contains $alba2)[<div>One petal of the mandala is paler than the rest, and cooler when you press a finger to it.</div>
(link: "Attend to the petal")[(set: $alba to $alba + (a: $alba2))<div class="revelation-box" data-alba="2"><em>‘$alba2’</em></div><strong class="alba-counter">THE SECOND LINE OF THREE</strong>]
]
[[Step through the mandala|Himalayan Return]]
]

:: Himalayan Return [outdoor street-night] {"position":"1500,2400","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Player completed the Himalayan trip. The mandala carries them home.
     Dean Street is reached with the mantra in the notebook and a
     permanent change to the critic's response (see The critic's
     judgement passage). -->
<script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssAudio&&window.dssAudio.passageWhoosh)window.dssAudio.passageWhoosh();},200);</script>
<div>
Dean Street. You remember something, not much, about mountains, thunder and nothing else.
</div>

[[Dean Street|Dean Street]]

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     v2-EXPANSION — NAZCA, PERU (Pillar of Mercy / upper right)
     5 passages: Nazca Approach → Walking the Pampa → The Ridge → The
     Centre → Nazca Return. Gift: tracing of the hummingbird geoglyph.
     Soho-responds: Lackland (the agent in his back room).
     ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

:: Himalayan Turn-Back [outdoor] {"position":"1100,2400","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Player turned back from the foothills. Half-mantra stays in their
     pocket. $tonightsWorld resets so they can try again from the
     Pillars portal. Returns straight to Dean Street. -->
(set: $tonightsWorld to "")\
<div>
You come to on Dean Street with a napkin, cold in your fist, still frozen at one corner. What you gathered of the mantra is written there. The rest is waiting somewhere you were too warm to go.
</div>

[[Dean Street|Dean Street]]

:: Nazca Approach [dream nazca] {"position":"1700,2200","size":"100,100"}
<div id="nz-container"></div>
<div>
A bus stopped on a coastal road, sunning like a Guanay cormorant, and the Pacific on its wing growing pewter. Nobody else is getting off for Nazca.

It sets you down at a bluff cantina where a slip road cambers into the interior. Against the wall, leans a propeller from a Cessna with its blade chipped at the tip; a man in a gaucho hat spills out of its shade.

‘Stay cool,’ he says. ‘Out there, there is no shadow.’
</div>

<div>[[Out onto the pampa|Walking the Pampa]]</div>

:: Walking the Pampa [dream nazca] {"position":"1900,2200","size":"100,100"}
(set: $sobriety to $sobriety - 6)\
<div>
He’s right, the Pampa’s thin and dry as parchment, as if you might tear through it if you breathe too heavy.

You’re walking a line where the stones have been cleared from the ground. It is, clearly, the work of human hands and yet the predictable ratio of its curve suggests the vision of some higher architect.

Someway to your right is a high ridge. From there you could see.
</div>
<span class="inventory-note">SOBRIETY -6</span>

<div>[[Climb the ridge|The Ridge]]
[[Turn back from the heat|Nazca Turn-Back]]</div>

:: The Ridge [dream nazca] {"position":"2100,2200","size":"100,100"}
(set: $sobriety to $sobriety - 6)\
<div>
You climb it. Almost an hour of thirsty rock, then a flat top. From here, you can see.

The line you were walking is a wing. A beak needles the haze on the horizon; there’s a tail that splits into bars like a tuning fork. That is a hummingbird.
</div>

<div>[[Down to the centre, where a car is waiting|Nazca Race]]</div>

:: The Centre — Nazca [dream nazca centre] {"position":"2300,2200","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Completion passage for Nazca. Gold-linework hummingbird geoglyph
     reveal on click. Sets $nazcaTracing + adds to $worldsVisited +
     clears $tonightsWorld + persists in localStorage. -->
<div>
You walk into the middle of the bird where its heart would be. The black car’s there, restoring its engine’s cool. (if: $nazcaRaceWon is true)[It got here after you.](else:)[It got here first.] Beside it is a cairn of sorts, a pile of screwball paper.

You recognise its driver from the shadow of the Cessna blade, he sits in the car’s open door, legs out and a notebook on his knee. He writes nothing, just tears the pages out and tosses them several feet onto the pile. They land and settle perfectly, every time.

‘That’s yours,’ he says, casting a paper ball that seemed as trackless as the others. You lift it off the cairn and prise it flat. The bird is on it, with you as a little black dot at its quavering heart.
</div>

(link: "Take the tracing")[
(set: $nazcaTracing to true)\
(if: $nazcaRaceWon is true)[(set: $confidence to ($statGain: $confidence, 8))(display: "Bars Now")<div class="inventory-note">MORALE +8</div>]\
(unless: $worldsVisited contains "nazca")[(set: $worldsVisited to $worldsVisited + (a: "nazca"))]
(set: $tonightsWorld to "")\
<script>if(window.dssMarkWorldSeen)window.dssMarkWorldSeen("nazca");</script>\
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">TRACING</div>
<div class="item-name">The Hummingbird, from above</div>
</div>

