<!-- ALBA 2 ATTEND-MOMENT (phase 2, 2026-09-01): the second line is latent in every world centre,
     earned by a quiet attend-choice in the world's register (the Green Sea "Listen" pattern). Pink draft. -->
(unless: $alba contains $alba2)[<div>
Among the thousand eyes you recognise two; she wants to give you something.
</div>
(link: "Meet her look")[(set: $alba to $alba + (a: $alba2))<div class="revelation-box" data-alba="2"><em>‘$alba2’</em></div><strong class="alba-counter">THE SECOND LINE OF THREE</strong>]
]
<!-- 2026-10-08 (Dr Quill, option A): no Return screen; the vision goes straight into the Synthesis. His Ezekiel Return line, kept: "Dean Street again, that vision imprinted on your vision like a motherless duck." -->
(set: $fetchSeen to true)[[Come back|The Synthesis]]
]

:: Third Pillar Portal [dream] {"position":"500,2200","size":"100,100"}
<!-- v2-expansion: world-roll happens in JS so the localStorage lifetime
     tracking can actually guarantee replay variety. Hidden Harlowe
     links are pre-rendered for each world; JS picks one (this-
     playthrough exclusion + lifetime exclusion) and clicks the right
     hidden link. No undocumented Harlowe internals; uses only standard
     DOM dispatch. Falls back to a "Back to the Pillars" link when the
     pool is empty. -->
(set: $crossedThreshold to true)\
(set: $lostToDrink to $lostToDrink - (a: "pillar"))\
<div id="tp-container"></div>

<!-- Visited-list span — JS reads this to know which worlds have been
     completed this playthrough. Harlowe prints arrays as comma-joined
     strings, perfect for JS to split on. -->
<span id="dss-pt-unlocked" style="display:none">(print: $inisToldOfPillars)</span>
<span id="dss-pt-visited" style="display:none">(print: $worldsVisited)</span>
(display: "Key Guards")<span id="dss-pt-key" style="display:none">(print: $dreamKey)</span>
<div>A third pillar rises. It is knit of the storm’s blue runoff and the Straits of Gibraltar; a third between the Pillars of Hercules.</div>
(if: $dreamKey is not "")[<div id="dss-pt-steer" style="display:none">The (print: $keyNames's ($dreamKey)) in your pocket seems to heat with some occulted energy. It is taking you somewhere altogether elsewhere.</div>]\
<!-- Hidden Harlowe links — JS clicks the matching one to navigate. The
     visible link text is the world identifier so JS can find it.
     The whole container is display:none so the player never sees them.
     (2026-10-06: the line breaks between these notes were six blank lines on the page.) -->\
<!-- POCKET-KEY CROSSING: the key is spent, with no time charge.
     HARLOWE GOTCHA (found 2026-09-01): Harlowe ignores clicks on a tw-link
     that has no layout box, so a display:none container made every hidden
     link here (and the fallback link) dead to targetLink.click(). The roll
     is now parked off-screen instead: laid out, clipped, never seen. -->\
<div id="dss-portal-roll" aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;top:0;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;pointer-events:none">
(link: "himalayas-go")[(display: "Spend Held Key")(go-to: "Airport Pub")]
(link: "nazca-go")[(display: "Spend Held Key")(go-to: "Nazca Approach")]
(link: "easter-go")[(display: "Spend Held Key")(go-to: "Easter Island Shore")]
(link: "pyramid-go")[(display: "Spend Held Key")(go-to: "Pyramid Mouth")]
(link: "ezekiel-go")[(display: "Spend Held Key")(go-to: "The Plain of Chebar")]
</div>

<div>
The third blue post rears skyward like a rearing hippocamp. The portal was here already; it takes some people longer than others to notice.
</div>

<div id="dss-portal-action"></div>

<!-- TURN-BACKS (2026-09-14). The key names the world; these are the two ways
     that can come to nothing. Both pink for Sam. Each carries its own way out,
     so neither can strand the player. -->
<div id="dss-portal-seen" style="display:none">
<div>
You’ve seen this one before, you think; the flesh cools under your palms.<!-- Retired timing instruction: Something else, then, and some other night. -->
</div>

(link: "Back to the Pillars")[(set: $pillarsNoAuto to true)(go-to: "Entering The Pillars of Hercules")]
</div>

<div id="dss-portal-notyet" style="display:none">
<div>
The glass eye that you hold does nothing here. Not yet. There are other dreams to have before it opens. Seek their keys among the night’s detritus.
</div>

(link: "Back to the Pillars")[(set: $pillarsNoAuto to true)(go-to: "Entering The Pillars of Hercules")]
</div>

<div id="dss-portal-fallback" style="display:none">
<!-- 2026-10-06 (Dr Quill): no key or no word from Inis, no pillar. The Pillars never links here in that case;
     if the Portal is ever reached so, the script below sends the player straight back to the pub. No words. -->

(link: "Back to the Pillars")[(set: $pillarsNoAuto to true)(go-to: "Entering The Pillars of Hercules")]
</div>

<script>
(function(){
  var all = ["himalayas","nazca","easter","pyramid","ezekiel"];
  // Lifetime list comes straight from localStorage — no Harlowe bridge.
  var lifetime = []; // 2026-10-09 structure pass: a fresh night is a first night; only this night's worlds count here.
  // Per-playthrough list comes from the hidden span Harlowe just rendered.
  var visitedRaw = (document.getElementById('dss-pt-visited').textContent || '');
  var visited = visitedRaw.split(',').map(function(s){return s.trim();})
    .filter(function(s){return s.length > 0 && all.indexOf(s) >= 0;});

  // ── THE KEY DECIDES (2026-09-14) ─────────────────────────────────────────
  // No roll any more. The pocket-key names the world and nothing else does, so
  // which world you get is a thing the player chose in Soho, not a dice throw.
  // Different unfinished worlds can be completed in the same night.
  // Gifts persist across nights; entering alone does not complete a world.
  //
  // Ezekiel is held back until the other four are walked. It is not a site like
  // the others — it is the vision they are evidence for — and it is the one
  // world you cannot turn back from, so it comes last.
  var FINAL = "ezekiel";
  var finalReady = all.every(function(w) {
    return w === FINAL || lifetime.indexOf(w) >= 0 || visited.indexOf(w) >= 0;
  });

  var actionEl = document.getElementById('dss-portal-action');
  var fallbackEl = document.getElementById('dss-portal-fallback');
  var seenEl = document.getElementById('dss-portal-seen');
  var notyetEl = document.getElementById('dss-portal-notyet');
  if (!actionEl) return;

  var keyEl = document.getElementById('dss-pt-key');
  var held = keyEl ? (keyEl.textContent || '').trim() : '';
  var chosen = (held && window.DSS_KEY_WORLDS) ? window.DSS_KEY_WORLDS[held] : null;

  function turnBack(el) {
    if (el) el.style.display = 'block';
    else if (fallbackEl) fallbackEl.style.display = 'block';
  }
  // No key, or a key with no world behind it: the column has nothing to open.
  if (!chosen || document.getElementById("dss-pt-unlocked").textContent.trim() !== "true") {
    turnBack(fallbackEl);
    setTimeout(function(){ var back = fallbackEl && fallbackEl.querySelector('tw-link'); if (back) back.click(); }, 0);
    return;
  }
  // Gifts record completion permanently; unfinished worlds remain available.
  if (lifetime.indexOf(chosen) >= 0 || visited.indexOf(chosen) >= 0) { turnBack(seenEl); return; }
  if (chosen === FINAL && !finalReady) { turnBack(notyetEl); return; }

  var steerEl = document.getElementById('dss-pt-steer');
  if (steerEl) steerEl.style.display = 'block';

  // Find the hidden Harlowe link whose text matches "<world>-go".
  var hiddenLinks = document.querySelectorAll('#dss-portal-roll tw-link');
  var targetLink = null;
  for (var i = 0; i < hiddenLinks.length; i++) {
    hiddenLinks[i].setAttribute('tabindex', '-1'); // off-screen: keep out of the tab order
    var txt = (hiddenLinks[i].textContent || '').trim();
    if (txt === chosen + '-go') { targetLink = hiddenLinks[i]; break; }
  }
  if (!targetLink) {
    if (fallbackEl) fallbackEl.style.display = 'block';
    return;
  }

  // Build a visible "Step through" link that triggers the hidden
  // Harlowe navigation. Uses <tw-link> so it picks up Harlowe's link
  // styling automatically. .click() on the hidden tw-link triggers
  // Harlowe's internal passage navigation.
  var box = document.createElement('div');
  box.className = 'choice-box';
  var link = document.createElement('tw-link');
  link.setAttribute('role', 'link');
  link.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
  link.style.cursor = 'pointer';
  link.textContent = 'Step through';
  link.addEventListener('click', function(){ targetLink.click(); });
  link.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
    if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); targetLink.click(); }
  });
  box.appendChild(link);
  actionEl.appendChild(box);
})();
</script>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     v2-EXPANSION — HIMALAYAN TRIP (Pillar of Mildness / centre)
     Prototype world for the Three Pillars portal system. Five passages:
     Airport Pub → The Road to India → Foothills → The Mountain → The Cave.
     Gift: completed mantra ($mantraComplete). Returns to Dean Street via
     Himalayan Return with dust-on-boots prose. All prose drafted in
     .claude-draft (bright pink) — Dr Quill to rework.
     ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

:: The Sanctum [dream sanctum] {"position":"500,2700","size":"100,100"}
<span id="dss-end-sanctum" hidden></span><script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssEndgameStage)window.dssEndgameStage("sanctum",document.getElementById("dss-end-sanctum"));},0);</script>\
<!-- v2-expansion: the 6th world. Accessible only via The Synthesis,
     which requires lifetime 5/5 gifts. The mythic inner sanctum — the
     true Pillars of Hercules, beyond Carthage, where the protagonist
     meets the figure who has been guiding him through every world.
     This is scaffold prose; Dr Quill to rework. -->
<div>
The room is the shape of the long table that fills it. It is not dark, there are no shadows. The light, such as it is, draws from no source, is more a sort of background radiation, leftover, perhaps, from Genesis 1:3.

Your book is on the table; the GREAT HAM, hooded, monkish, looms above it.

‘It was all true,’ he says. ‘Who’d ever believe it?’

A kettle comes to the boil in a cold kitchen.
</div>

<div>
He opens the book at its end where, in your own hand but not by your own hand, is written this:

//You can go now. Everything is true.//

‘Take your own advice,’ he says and smiles.
</div>

<!-- 2026-10-08 (Dr Quill): "once you reach the sanctum there should be no return ... and you don't sit anymore". Sanctum and Sitting are one screen with one link into the endgame; the Sitting and Alt-Dawn passages are deleted. -->
(set: $sanctumDone to true)<div class="choice-box">[[Go now|The Fetch]]</div>

:: The Synthesis [dream synthesis] {"position":"500,2500","size":"100,100"}
<span id="dss-end-synthesis" hidden></span><script>setTimeout(function(){if(window.dssEndgameStage)window.dssEndgameStage("synthesis",document.getElementById("dss-end-synthesis"));},0);</script>\
<!-- v2-expansion: the 6th-world ritual. Accessible only when all 5
     lifetime gifts have been earned (multi-playthrough payoff). Player
     performs the five gifts in sequence; on the fifth, the hexagram
     materialises and the door to the Sanctum opens. -->
<div>
You have everything you need: the mantra, the tracing, the glyph, the number and the vision. The three blue posts triangulate and plot the state of hyperstition where you stretch a singularity through several folds of Soho’s fabric, like a needle seen from above by a dancing angel.<!-- Retired five-night instruction: Five gifts gathered across five nights, without knowing you were preparing. -->
</div>

(link: "Speak the mantra")[
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">MANTRA</div>
<div class="item-name">(print: 1 of $mantra) · (print: 2 of $mantra) · (print: 3 of $mantra) · (print: 4 of $mantra) · (print: 5 of $mantra) · (print: 6 of $mantra)</div>
</div>


(link: "Hold up the tracing")[
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">TRACING</div>
<div class="item-name">The Hummingbird, from above</div>
</div>


(link: "Remember the glyph")[
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">GLYPH</div>
<div class="item-name">A glyph in Rongorongo</div>
</div>


(link: "Hum the number")[
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">PROPORTION</div>
<div class="item-name">A resonant number</div>
</div>


(link: "Draw the wheel")[
<div class="item-box">
<div class="item-header">VISION</div>
<div class="item-name">The wheel-within-a-wheel</div>
</div>

<div>
You draw the wheel in the air, outer, then inner. The eyes around its rim open and watch you to the thin end of the gesture.
</div>
<div>
The three blue posts transhift into the scalene and by Pythagoras’ metempsychosis, which is true, multiply fivefold, and lay themselves in the gullies of the pentagram you drew with gathered lilies over Soho.
</div>

