}

:: The Deal [venue-lackland] {"position":"1300,1150","size":"100,100"}
<!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam: "should it even be possible to sell it? like a rare ending"): reached only from LACKLAND's near-yes on
     a later night (dssBookDeal). Provisional words in pink; he decides what the sale means. Shaking hands leaves the book
     with him ($bookSold; the Dawn knows); keeping it is the other road ($bookDeclined). -->
<span>He lights a cigarette and does not answer for a long time. Then he turns an envelope and writes on its back.</span>

<span>It is less than you hoped and more than you have ever had.</span>

|dealchoice>[(link: "Shake his hand")[(set: $bookSold to true)(replace: ?dealchoice)[<span class="dss-refusal" data-k="deal" data-who="LACKLAND" data-yes="1" hidden>‘Leave it with me.’</span><span>He keeps the manuscript. You go down the two doglegs of stairs with nothing in your bag.</span>

[[Back to the street|Dean Street]]]]
(link: "Keep it")[(set: $bookDeclined to true)(replace: ?dealchoice)[<span>You put it back in your bag. He shrugs, as if he had expected nothing else.</span>

[[Back to the street|Dean Street]]]]]

:: Book Footer [footer] {"position":"3650,2600","size":"100,100"}
{<!-- 2026-10-14 (Sam: the manuscript lost along the way; provisional words in pink for him): leave a venue very drunk
     (sobriety under 25) and, one time in two, the book stays behind (once a night). NEXT and a Get Directions slip lead
     back; entering that venue gets it back. Left two laps, it is gone to the man outside Foyles (Alley: Charing Cross
     Road), who wants the coin or the pocket key for it. $bookAt: "" in your bag, a venue id, or "foyles". -->
(unless: $bookAt is a string)[(set: $bookAt to "")](unless: $bookLent is a string)[(set: $bookLent to "")](unless: $bookLastVenue is a string)[(set: $bookLastVenue to "")](unless: $bookLeftLap is a number)[(set: $bookLeftLap to 0)]<!-- 2026-10-24 sweep: Dean Street displays this passage itself, before its bag line and pitch question, and stamps $bookRollLap; as a footer it then skips the hub roll for that lap. Before, the roll ran after the body, so the lap the book was left behind read "In your bag, you have your novel" and offered readers over the slip saying it was still at the pub (played live). -->(unless: $bookRollLap is a number)[(set: $bookRollLap to -1)]
(set: _bvh to (dm: "venue-pillars", "pillars", "venue-cecilcourt", "cecil", "venue-french", "french", "venue-colony", "colony", "venue-ronnies", "ronnies", "venue-coach", "coach", "venue-trishas", "trishas", "venue-lackland", "lackland", "venue-chippy", "chippy"))
(set: _bplace to (dm: "pillars", "the Pillars", "cecil", "Cecil Court", "french", "the French", "colony", "the Colony", "ronnies", "Ronnie’s", "coach", "the Coach", "trishas", "Trisha’s", "lackland", "LACKLAND’S office", "chippy", "the chippy"))
(set: _bhere to "")(for: each _t, ...(passage:)'s tags)[(if: _bvh contains _t)[(set: _bhere to _bvh's (_t))]]
(if: _bhere is not "")[(if: $bookAt is _bhere)[(set: $bookAt to "")<span class="book-note-src" hidden><span>Someone has kept it behind the bar for you. You put the book back in your bag.</span></span>](else-if: ($bookAt is "") and ($bookSold is not true) and ($bookLostTonight is not true) and ($bookLent is "") and ($sobriety < 15))[<!-- 2026-10-25 (Sam, design note 5.4): in the room, drunk enough that the book will stay here when you leave --><span class="book-note-src" hidden><span>You are too far gone to keep track of your bag. When you leave, the book will stay here.</span></span>](set: $bookLastVenue to _bhere)]
(else-if: (passage:)'s tags contains "hub" and ($bookRollLap is not $returns))[(if: ($bookLastVenue is not "") and ($bookAt is "") and ($bookSold is not true) and ($bookLostTonight is not true) and ($bookLent is "") and ($sobriety < 15))[<!-- 2026-10-25 (Sam, design note 5.4): no coin; under 25 (2026-10-28, playtest note 27: under 15, the warning 15 to 24) the book is always left behind -->(set: $bookAt to $bookLastVenue)(set: $bookLostTonight to true)(set: $bookLeftLap to $returns)(print: "<span class='book-note-src' data-go='" + $bookAt + "' hidden><span>Halfway down the street your bag feels lighter. Your book is still at " + (_bplace's ($bookAt)) + ".</span></span>")](else-if: ($bookAt is not "") and ($bookAt is not "foyles") and ($returns >= $bookLeftLap + 2))[(set: $bookAt to "foyles")<span class="book-note-src" data-go="foyles" hidden><span>Your book has been gone too long. Someone will have walked off with it by now. There is a man outside Foyles who buys anything.</span></span>](else-if: ($bookAt is "") and ($bookSold is not true) and ($bookLostTonight is not true) and ($bookLent is "") and ($bookWarned is not true) and ($sobriety >= 15) and ($sobriety < 25))[<!-- 2026-10-25 (Sam, design note 5.4): the warning on the street before the book is lost, once a night --><span class="book-note-src" hidden><span>Drink more and you’ll start losing things. Where is your book?</span></span>(set: $bookWarned to true)](set: $bookLastVenue to "")]
<script>setTimeout(function(){ if (window.dssBookNote) window.dssBookNote(); }, 500);</script>
}

