:: BEVAN’s pigeon [outdoor]
<!-- 2026-10-25: Sam's approved text with the listed typo fixes. No completion flag on leaving. -->
(unless: $helpedBevan is true)[<div class="bevan-pigeon-request">Bevan Glyndŵr opens his coat and shows you a pigeon in his pocket, with one wing broken.<br>
‘I should guess it was hit by a car,’ he mumbles, looking down at it with such love and pity in his eyes that you could imagine, for a moment, that his own soul took the place of the pigeon’s, through sheer force of his empathetic will.<br>
‘I can’t do it. Will you?’</div>
[[Take the bird|Helping BEVAN]]
[[Leave it with him|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]
](else:)[[[Back outside the chippy|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]]

:: Helping BEVAN [outdoor]
(unless: $helpedBevan is true)[(set: $helpedBevan to true)<div class="bevan-pigeon-result">You take the bird from him.<br>
Afterwards, he wraps it in a newspaper. You stay while he folds the sheets carefully.<br>
‘You’re looking for LILY, I think?’<br>
You ask how he knows her.<br>
‘Wales is not a big place. Give or take a tide, it's about as big as Wales. She stops by here, you know, on her way home; she'll probably be passing by later.’<br>
He puts the wrapped bird in the bin among the other things abandoned, fishes and chips, in their newspaper coats.<br>
‘You might catch her,’ he says.</div>]
[[Back outside the chippy|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]

:: Waiting outside the chippy [outdoor]
<!-- 2026-10-25 (Sam): LILY never comes. Waits are client-side only: no passage refresh,
     calls, night clock or event progression. Later the same day (Sam): each finished wait sobers you
     a little and costs a little morale, through the hidden .bw-tick link (morale floors at 20). Five narrated
     minutes take five real seconds; each successive interval adds five of each.
     Elapsed waiting is labelled without a clock time. Rain and blur run only while waiting. -->
(if: $helpedBevan is true)[<section class="bevan-waiting-clock" aria-label="Waiting outside the chippy">
<div id="fc-container"></div>
<div class="bevan-waiting">WAITING FOR LILY</div>

<p class="bw-elapsed" aria-live="off">0 minutes waiting.</p>
<p class="bw-status" role="status">LILY has not come.</p>
<button class="bw-wait" type="button">Keep waiting · 5 minutes</button>
<span class="bw-leave">[[Leave|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]</span>
</section><span class="bw-tick" aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;top:0;">(link-repeat: "·")[(set: $sobriety to ($statGain: $sobriety, 4))(if: $confidence > 20)[(set: $confidence to (max: 20, ($statLoss: $confidence, 3)))](display: "Bars Now")]</span>
<style>
.dss-threshold:has(.bevan-waiting-clock){z-index:9011;background:transparent;pointer-events:none;}
.dss-room-prose:has(.bevan-waiting-clock){background:transparent!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;pointer-events:none;}
.bevan-waiting-clock{color:#dccaa7;font:16px/1.5 Georgia,serif;text-align:center;position:fixed;left:50%;bottom:24px;transform:translateX(-50%);width:min(520px,92vw);margin:0;padding:20px 12px;box-sizing:border-box;z-index:9012;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(4,4,8,.82) 35%);pointer-events:auto;text-shadow:0 2px 6px #000;}
.bevan-waiting{font:16px Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#ead8b4;}
.bevan-waiting-clock p{margin:10px 0;}
.bevan-waiting-clock br{display:none;}
.bw-street-scene canvas{will-change:filter;transform-origin:center;}
@media(max-width:600px){.bevan-waiting-clock{bottom:12px;padding:16px 8px;}}
.bw-wait{font:inherit;color:#d4b37c;background:transparent;border:1px solid #8b744d;padding:10px 18px;cursor:pointer;}
.bw-wait:disabled{opacity:.65;cursor:wait;}
.bw-wait:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #e0c493;outline-offset:4px;}
.bw-leave{display:block;margin:20px auto 0;background:transparent;border:0;color:#d4b37c;font:inherit;cursor:pointer;}
.bw-status{min-height:1.5em;}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  var root=[].filter.call(document.querySelectorAll('.bevan-waiting-clock'),function(el){return !el.closest('.dss-ghost');}).pop();if(!root)return;
  // The canvas sits outside tw-story's stacking context. Hoist only the visual UI;
  // its Leave action proxies the real Harlowe link kept with its passage.
  var anchor=document.createElement('span');root.parentNode.insertBefore(anchor,root);
  var leaveSource=root.querySelector('.bw-leave');root.parentNode.insertBefore(leaveSource,root);
  leaveSource.style.cssText='position:absolute;left:-9999px;top:0;';
  var tickLink=anchor.parentNode.querySelector('.bw-tick tw-link');
  var leaveLink=leaveSource.querySelector('tw-link'),leaveButton=document.createElement('button');
  leaveButton.type='button';leaveButton.className='bw-leave';leaveButton.textContent='Leave';
  leaveButton.addEventListener('click',function(){if(leaveLink)leaveLink.click();});root.appendChild(leaveButton);
  document.body.appendChild(root);
  var button=root.querySelector('.bw-wait');
  var elapsed=root.querySelector('.bw-elapsed'),status=root.querySelector('.bw-status');
  var rounds=0,total=0,running=false,raf=0,alive=true;
  root.dataset.waitActive='false';root.dataset.waitProgress='0';
  function clearFocus(){var c=document.querySelector('.bw-street-scene canvas');if(c){c.style.filter='none';c.style.transform='none';}}
  function stop(){alive=false;root.dataset.waitActive='false';root.dataset.waitProgress='0';clearFocus();cancelAnimationFrame(raf);observer.disconnect();root.remove();}
  button.addEventListener('click',function(e){
    e.stopPropagation();if(running||!alive)return;
    running=true;rounds++;var minutes=5*rounds,duration=minutes*1000,start=performance.now(),before=total;
    button.disabled=true;button.textContent='Waiting…';
    status.textContent=minutes+' minutes pass.';root.dataset.waitActive='true';root.dataset.waitProgress='0';
    function tick(now){
      if(!alive||!root.isConnected){stop();return;}
      var progress=Math.min(1,Math.max(0,(now-start)/duration)),shown=before+minutes*progress;
      root.dataset.waitProgress=String(progress);
      if(progress<1){raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick);return;}
      total=before+minutes;running=false;button.disabled=false;if(tickLink)tickLink.click();root.dataset.waitActive='false';root.dataset.waitProgress='0';clearFocus();
      elapsed.textContent=total+' minutes waiting.';
      status.textContent='LILY has not come.';
      button.textContent='Keep waiting · '+(5*(rounds+1))+' minutes';
    }
    raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  });
  var observer=new MutationObserver(function(){if(!anchor.isConnected)stop();});
  observer.observe(document.querySelector('tw-story'),{childList:true,subtree:true});
})();
</script>
](else:)[[[Leave|Approach Chinese Fish and Chips]]]

:: Preview Himalayas [system]
<!-- PREVIEW LINKS (2026-09-23; carried over from the unmerged preview-launcher branch 2026-10-26, Sam). The game URL with ?start=himalayas (or nazca,
     easter, pyramid, ezekiel) lands on the matching Preview passage below; the
     boot hook that reads the URL lives in sync_html.py, the launcher page is
     preview.html. Each Preview passage seeds only what the story would have
     set by the time the third pillar opened that world: Inis has told of the
     pillars, the threshold is crossed, the world's own key is spent. Then it
     goes straight to the world's first passage. Nothing else about the night
     is invented, so a preview night otherwise starts fresh. -->
(display: "Key Guards")\
(set: $inisToldOfPillars to true)(set: $crossedThreshold to true)\
(set: $keyLighter to "spent")(set: $dreamKey to "")\
(go-to: "Airport Pub")

